</section>
<section id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Empirical highlights.</h5>

<div id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">On clinical diagnosis with 1,500 cases spanning <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="100{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">100{+}</annotation></semantics></math> diseases, <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MACI}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>MACI</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MACI}</annotation></semantics></math> improves Acc@1 by <span id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">+3.9 pp</span> over majority vote and <span id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">+3.7 pp</span> over fixed-contentiousness debate, reduces calibration error (ECE <span id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.081</span> vs. 0.103), and uses <span id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">19% fewer</span> generation tokens. A cross-domain study on news bias (619 articles) shows portability: the same controls narrow the partisan gap by <span id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">68%</span> without domain tuning. <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MACI}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>MACI</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MACI}</annotation></semantics></math> also translates residual uncertainty into <em id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.6" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">precision RAG</em> plans that specify what to retrieve next to improve decision quality.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px6" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Contributions.</h5>

<div id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We operationalize these ideas into five contributions:</p>
<ol id="S1.I1" class="ltx_enumerate" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.2em;">
<li id="S1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="S1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Dual control.</em> Two-dial orchestration with information-theoretic stopping, where <math id="S1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(t)</annotation></semantics></math> is nonincreasing and plateau tests terminate within bounded rounds (Lem. <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 (Monotonicity under gated averaging). ‣ M.2 Monotonicity of dispersion ‣ Appendix M Plateau Guarantees" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, Prop. <a href="#Thmproposition2" title="Proposition 2 (Termination in 𝑂(1/𝜀) expected rounds). ‣ M.4 Termination of the plateau controller ‣ Appendix M Plateau Guarantees" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="S1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Judge robustness.</em> <math id="S1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CRIT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>CRIT</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CRIT}</annotation></semantics></math> is order invariant and stable under cross-family judge swaps (Appx. <a href="#A5.SS7" title="E.7 CRIT Reliability and Role in MACI ‣ Appendix E CRIT: Cross-Family Argument Quality Evaluator" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.7</span></a>; <math id="S1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n{=}100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n{=}100</annotation></semantics></math>, 2–3% winner flips; <math id="S1.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha{=}0.68" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.68</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha{=}0.68</annotation></semantics></math>); we use it as a soft weight and part of a compound stop rule, not a hard oracle.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="S1.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Targeted acquisition.</em> Systematic collaboration yields predictions together with precision RAG plans for underspecified problems.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="S1.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Empirical validation.</em> Improvements in accuracy, calibration, and efficiency across two domains, with complete ablations and transcripts.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px7" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Evaluator reliability.</h5>

<div id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We rely on <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CRIT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>CRIT</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CRIT}</annotation></semantics></math>, a cross-family judge that scores evidence-, logic-, and relevance-grounded argument quality. We validate order invariance and judge-swap stability (<math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n{=}100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n{=}100</annotation></semantics></math>; 2–3% winner flips) and report tentatively acceptable agreement (Krippendorff’s <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha{=}0.68" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.68</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha{=}0.68</annotation></semantics></math>). We therefore use <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CRIT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>CRIT</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CRIT}</annotation></semantics></math> as a soft aggregation weight and as part of a compound stop rule, rather than as a hard oracle. Stability holds with high-capability judges; weaker or poorly aligned judges may require larger <math id="S1.SS0.SSS0.Px7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, tighter thresholds, or periodic human audits (Appx. <a href="#A5.SS7" title="E.7 CRIT Reliability and Role in MACI ‣ Appendix E CRIT: Cross-Family Argument Quality Evaluator" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.7</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">2 </span>Related Work</h2>

<section id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Multi-agent debate and orchestration.</h5>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Debate-style prompting aims to surface errors through agent
opposition <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Irving et al., 2018</a>)</cite>, yet implementations often collapse to majority opinions or underperform strong single
models <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2024b</a>; <a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Smit et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Estornell and Liu, 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Choi et al., 2025b</a>)</cite>.
For example, Liang et al. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liang et al., 2024</a>)</cite> maintain fixed adversarial intensity throughout, wasting tokens when contention becomes unproductive. Diverse Multi-Agent Debate <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al., 2025</a>)</cite> varies agent prompting styles but lacks behavioral adaptation within debates. Recent audits reveal that multi-agent systems frequently fail without systematic orchestration <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cemri et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, motivating principled control mechanisms.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S1.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ Guarantees and scheduler. ‣ 1 Introduction" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> reveals a critical gap: existing methods provide either no control or single-axis control (fixed/varied debate intensity), but none combine independent information gating with scheduled behavioral transitions.
<em id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Aggregation methods</em> sample diverse responses but aggregate without deliberation, causing performance degradation as answer spaces
grow <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Choi et al., 2025b</a>)</cite>. <em id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Fixed-stance debate</em>
methods maintain constant intensity, unable to transition from exploratory disagreement to consolidative synthesis.
<math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MACI}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>MACI</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MACI}</annotation></semantics></math> addresses both limitations: an information dial filters evidence by quality while a behavior dial schedules contentiousness from high to low, with information-theoretic stopping that detects convergence plateaus rather than relying on heuristic round limits. <span id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">To our knowledge, no prior work provides independent controls over information quality and behavioral stance.</span></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Computational paradigms and capability trade-offs.</h5>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Transformers <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Vaswani et al., 2017</a>)</cite> required orders of magnitude more computation than RNNs but unlocked scaling laws <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kaplan et al., 2020</a>)</cite>; large language models <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Brown et al., 2020</a>)</cite> continue this trend. <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MACI}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>MACI</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MACI}</annotation></semantics></math> follows this paradigm: systematic orchestration requires overhead, but provides measurable gains in accuracy, calibration, and epistemic humility. For high-stakes applications, reliability justifies cost.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Ensemble methods and aggregation.</h5>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Self-Consistency <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2023</a>)</cite> and majority voting aggregate sampled chains with fixed behavior. Mixture-of-Agents <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2024a</a>; <a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2025</a>)</cite> improves performance via layered ensembles but under-specifies convergence beyond heuristic rounds. These methods assume weak error correlation and rarely specify stopping criteria. On short-horizon multiple-choice tasks, voting can dominate when answer spaces are small <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Choi et al., 2025b</a>)</cite>, but performance degrades as dimensionality grows (Appendix <a href="#A11" title="Appendix K Why Majority Voting Fails on Open-Ended Diagnosis" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">K</span></a>). MACI differs by using information-theoretic signals (disagreement, overlap, evidence quality) to drive active deliberation with plateau-based stopping.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Control and stopping in AI systems.</h5>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Control-theoretic approaches in reinforcement learning use measured feedback to adjust policy parameters <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Recht, 2019</a>)</cite>. Active learning frameworks gate information acquisition based on uncertainty <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Settles, 2009</a>)</cite>. Our work extends these ideas to multi-agent reasoning: the moderator tracks four signals and adjusts behavioral stance when progress plateaus, analogous to adaptive control in dynamical systems. Prior debate work lacks this closed-loop structure, relying instead on fixed interaction patterns or ad hoc stopping rules.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Initialization and few-shot learning.</h5>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Bayesian <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xie et al., 2022</a>)</cite>, meta-learning <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dai et al., 2023</a>)</cite>, and optimization-as-inference <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">von Oswald et al., 2023</a>)</cite> perspectives explain in-context learning. Selection and weighting strategies adapt which demonstrations matter <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hong et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2024c</a>)</cite>. We use lightweight information-theoretic metrics (pattern density, prior-target mismatch) to initialize debate parameters. Appendix <a href="#A6" title="Appendix F Adaptive Initialization Strategy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F</span></a> validates these heuristics on controlled tasks; broader ICL theory appears in concurrent work.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px6" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Evaluation with LLM judges.</h5>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Independent LLM judges are appealing, but evaluators can exhibit self-preference bias, especially when sharing a family with the debaters <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Panickssery et al., 2024</a>)</cite>. Moreover, recent scalable-oversight studies report that weak-judge regimes yield inconsistent gains <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kenton et al., 2024</a>)</cite>. <em id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Compounding this,</em> LLMs lack robust self-validation for constraint adherence and reasoning consistency <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bommasani et al., 2022</a>; <a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chang, 2025</a>)</cite>, a limitation loosely analogous to Gödel-style barriers <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gödel, 1967</a>)</cite> and supported empirically <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hong et al., 2024</a>)</cite>. Hence we use cross-family judges, mask agent identity, require span-grounded justifications, and aggregate small judge panels (<math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K{\geq}3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K{\geq}3</annotation></semantics></math>) with reliability weighting; judge-swap and order-swap checks, plus a CRIT-free controller variant, indicate that stopping and weights are not driven by a single evaluator.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3 </span>MACI: Information and Behavior Dials with Measurable Stopping</h2>

<section id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Goal.</h5>

<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Coordinate multiple LLM agents to explore meaningfully and then consolidate on well-supported conclusions with calibrated confidence under a fixed token budget. All notation is defined in Appx. <a href="#A4" title="Appendix D Information-Theoretic Signals for Debate Evaluation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Failures we address.</h5>

<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="S3.I1" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.2em;">
<li id="S3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Prior capture:</span> Single models fixate on high-frequency patterns and confirm early impressions.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Majority illusion:</span> Voting appears strong in multiple choice, but does not test the depth of reasoning or the quality of evidence.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Unregulated debate:</span> Contentiousness drifts, evidence quality is not gated, and stopping is ad hoc.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Cost sprawl:</span> Long chains consume budget without proportional gains.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Design summary.</h5>

<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MACI}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>MACI</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MACI}</annotation></semantics></math> exposes two independent controls. The <span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">information dial</span> <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\tau_{\mathit{Q}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tau_{\mathit{Q}})</annotation></semantics></math> gates which evidence agents may cite by enforcing a quality threshold. The <span id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">behavior dial</span> (<math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>CL</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CL}</annotation></semantics></math>) sets contentiousness, instructing agents how aggressively to challenge opponents.
A moderator tracks four signals—target-aligned evidence quality (<math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{Q}</annotation></semantics></math>), inter-agent disagreement (<math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\mathrm{JS}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>JS</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{JS}}</annotation></semantics></math>), support overlap (<math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>O</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{O}</annotation></semantics></math>), and argument quality (<math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CRIT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>CRIT</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CRIT}</annotation></semantics></math>)—and stops when they plateau jointly. The construction of the target prototype <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝜽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> used by <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{Q}</annotation></semantics></math> is detailed in Appx. <a href="#A4.SS1" title="D.1 Target prototype construction (𝜃) ‣ Appendix D Information-Theoretic Signals for Debate Evaluation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.1 </span>The Control Loop</h3>

<div id="S3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ Appendix C MACI Algorithm Specification" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> (in <span id="S3.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Appx. <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C MACI Algorithm Specification" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a></span>) shows the three-phase cycle.
Agents receive a composite anchor <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{(t)}=\big(\psi^{(t)},\,CL^{(t)},\,\tau_{\mathit{Q}}^{(t)},\,\tau_{\mathrm{CRIT}}^{(t)}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>CRIT</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{(t)}=\big(\psi^{(t)},\,CL^{(t)},\,\tau_{\mathit{Q}}^{(t)},\,\tau_{\mathrm{CRIT}}^{(t)}\big)</annotation></semantics></math>
that contains the history of curated debates, current contentiousness instruction, and evidence quality thresholds. Each agent produces claim-justification pairs with probability distribution <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{u}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{u}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> over the outcomes and evidence cited spans <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathcal{E}}_{u}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathcal{E}}_{u}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The moderator scores arguments with <span id="S3.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">CRIT</span> (Appendix <a href="#A5" title="Appendix E CRIT: Cross-Family Argument Quality Evaluator" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a>), computes evidence quality <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> for the cited spans, and admits only those satisfying both gates, <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q\geq\tau_{\text{Q}}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>Q</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q\geq\tau_{\text{Q}}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CRIT}\geq\tau_{\text{CRIT}}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>CRIT</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>CRIT</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CRIT}\geq\tau_{\text{CRIT}}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> (defaults in Appx. B.1); it then computes all signals and updates both dials.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2 </span>Four Measurement Signals</h3>

<section id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Notation.</h5>

<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> be finite outcome space, <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(\mathcal{Y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(\mathcal{Y})</annotation></semantics></math> the probability simplex. Two agents <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in\{A,B\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in\{A,B\}</annotation></semantics></math> alternate over rounds <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1,2,\ldots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1,2,\ldots</annotation></semantics></math>. Each outputs <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{u}^{(t)}\in\Delta(\mathcal{Y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{u}^{(t)}\in\Delta(\mathcal{Y})</annotation></semantics></math> and cites evidence spans <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathcal{E}}_{u}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathcal{E}}_{u}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Signal 1: Evidence quality (<math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{Q}</annotation></semantics></math>).</h5>

<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Measures alignment between cited evidence and target distribution using encoder embeddings:</p>
<table id="S3.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{Q}^{(t)}=\cos(\bar{\mathbf{e}}^{(t)},\boldsymbol{\theta}),\quad\bar{\mathbf{e}}^{(t)}=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{E}^{(t)}|}\sum_{e\in\mathcal{E}^{(t)}}\frac{\phi(e)}{\|\phi(e)\|}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐞</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐞</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{Q}^{(t)}=\cos(\bar{\mathbf{e}}^{(t)},\boldsymbol{\theta}),\quad\bar{\mathbf{e}}^{(t)}=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{E}^{(t)}|}\sum_{e\in\mathcal{E}^{(t)}}\frac{\phi(e)}{\|\phi(e)\|},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> collects the spans from <em id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">admitted</em> arguments in round <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝜽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> is the target prototype.
Rising <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{Q}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{Q}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> indicates convergence on task-relevant evidence.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Admission rule.</span> For each <em id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">candidate</em> argument <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> at round <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, we compute a per-argument evidence score <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> (analogous to (<a href="#S3.E1" title="Equation 1 ‣ Signal 1: Evidence quality (𝑄). ‣ 3.2 Four Measurement Signals ‣ 3 MACI: Information and Behavior Dials with Measurable Stopping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>), using only the spans cited by <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>). The moderator admits <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> iff it passes the <span id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">dual gate</span>:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}^{(t)}\,\geq\,\tau_{\mathit{Q}}(t)\quad\textbf{and}\quad\mathrm{CRIT}_{i}^{(t)}\,\geq\,\tau_{\mathrm{CRIT}}(t)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.448em" rspace="0.448em">≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msubsup><mi>CRIT</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.448em">≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>CRIT</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}^{(t)}\,\geq\,\tau_{\mathit{Q}}(t)\quad\textbf{and}\quad\mathrm{CRIT}_{i}^{(t)}\,\geq\,\tau_{\mathrm{CRIT}}(t).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">After admission, <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> aggregates all admitted spans and <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{Q}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{Q}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> summarizes the evidence quality of that batch. Default settings for <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\mathit{Q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\mathit{Q}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\mathrm{CRIT}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>CRIT</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\mathrm{CRIT}}</annotation></semantics></math> appear in Appx. B.1.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Signal 2: Disagreement (<math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\mathrm{JS}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>JS</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{JS}}</annotation></semantics></math>).</h5>

<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Jensen-Shannon divergence quantifies distributional disagreement:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\mathrm{JS}}^{(t)}=\tfrac{1}{2}\text{KL}(p_{A}^{(t)}\|m^{(t)})+\tfrac{1}{2}\text{KL}(p_{B}^{(t)}\|m^{(t)})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>JS</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mtext>KL</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mtext>KL</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{JS}}^{(t)}=\tfrac{1}{2}\text{KL}(p_{A}^{(t)}\|m^{(t)})+\tfrac{1}{2}\text{KL}(p_{B}^{(t)}\|m^{(t)}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S3.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{(t)}=\tfrac{1}{2}(p_{A}^{(t)}+p_{B}^{(t)})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{(t)}=\tfrac{1}{2}(p_{A}^{(t)}+p_{B}^{(t)}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\mathrm{JS}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>JS</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{JS}}</annotation></semantics></math> is symmetric and bounded in <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> when using log base <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>, and remains finite under disjoint support. Falling <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\mathrm{JS}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>JS</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{JS}}</annotation></semantics></math> tracks convergence; plateaus indicate exhausted productive disagreement (thresholds are selected on the development set; Appendix <a href="#A4" title="Appendix D Information-Theoretic Signals for Debate Evaluation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Signal 3: Support overlap (<math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>O</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{O}</annotation></semantics></math>).</h5>

<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Jaccard similarity of cited evidence sets:</p>
<table id="S3.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{O}^{(t)}=\frac{|\hat{\mathcal{E}}_{A}^{(t)}\cap\hat{\mathcal{E}}_{B}^{(t)}|}{|\hat{\mathcal{E}}_{A}^{(t)}\cup\hat{\mathcal{E}}_{B}^{(t)}|}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∩</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∪</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{O}^{(t)}=\frac{|\hat{\mathcal{E}}_{A}^{(t)}\cap\hat{\mathcal{E}}_{B}^{(t)}|}{|\hat{\mathcal{E}}_{A}^{(t)}\cup\hat{\mathcal{E}}_{B}^{(t)}|}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Rising overlap indicates agents grounding arguments in shared evidence rather than talking past each other. Combined with falling <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\mathrm{JS}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>JS</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{JS}}</annotation></semantics></math>, this signals genuine convergence rather than forced agreement.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Signal 4: Argument quality (<math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CRIT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>CRIT</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CRIT}</annotation></semantics></math>).</h5>

<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Cross-family LLM evaluator scores each argument on [0,1] for logical coherence, evidence support, and reasoning depth (Appendix <a href="#A5" title="Appendix E CRIT: Cross-Family Argument Quality Evaluator" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a>). The moderator maintains exponential moving average of per-agent quality:</p>
<table id="S3.E4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S3.E4X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E4X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Gamma_{u}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Gamma_{u}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E4X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\lambda\Gamma_{u}^{(t-1)}+(1-\lambda)\overline{\mathrm{CRIT}}_{u,t}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>CRIT</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\lambda\Gamma_{u}^{(t-1)}+(1-\lambda)\overline{\mathrm{CRIT}}_{u,t},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E4Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E4Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\omega_{u}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\omega_{u}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E4Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\Gamma_{u}^{(t)}+\epsilon}{\Gamma_{A}^{(t)}+\Gamma_{B}^{(t)}+2\epsilon}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\Gamma_{u}^{(t)}+\epsilon}{\Gamma_{A}^{(t)}+\Gamma_{B}^{(t)}+2\epsilon},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{u}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{u}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> weights agent <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>’s beliefs. Rising <math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CRIT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>CRIT</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CRIT}</annotation></semantics></math> indicates improving argument quality; agents producing consistently weak arguments receive less weight in the mixture.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.3 </span>Dual-Dial Control with Plateau Detection</h3>

<section id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Information gain.</h5>

<div id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Normalized entropy reduction of reliability-weighted mixture:</p>
<table id="S3.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{I}^{(t)}=\left[\frac{H(p^{(t-1)})-H(p^{(t)})}{\log|\mathcal{Y}|}\right]_{+},\quad p^{(t)}=\sum_{u}\omega_{u}^{(t)}p_{u}^{(t)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>u</mi></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{I}^{(t)}=\left[\frac{H(p^{(t-1)})-H(p^{(t)})}{\log|\mathcal{Y}|}\right]_{+},\quad p^{(t)}=\sum_{u}\omega_{u}^{(t)}p_{u}^{(t)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Falling <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{I}</annotation></semantics></math> indicates lower returns from continued debate.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Plateau detection via relative progress ratios.</h5>

<div id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Rather than fixed thresholds, we measure progress relative to remaining capacity:</p>
<table id="S3.E6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S3.E6X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E6X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r_{I}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r_{I}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E6X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\text{MA}_{w}(\hat{I}^{(t)})}{\text{MA}_{w}(H(p^{(t-1)})/\log|\mathcal{Y}|)+\eta}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mtext>MA</mtext><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mtext>MA</mtext><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\text{MA}_{w}(\hat{I}^{(t)})}{\text{MA}_{w}(H(p^{(t-1)})/\log|\mathcal{Y}|)+\eta},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E6Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E6Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r_{D}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r_{D}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E6Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\text{MA}_{w}([D_{\mathrm{JS}}^{(t-1)}-D_{\mathrm{JS}}^{(t)}]_{+})}{\text{MA}_{w}(D_{\mathrm{JS}}^{(t-1)})+\eta}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mtext>MA</mtext><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>JS</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>JS</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mtext>MA</mtext><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>JS</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\text{MA}_{w}([D_{\mathrm{JS}}^{(t-1)}-D_{\mathrm{JS}}^{(t)}]_{+})}{\text{MA}_{w}(D_{\mathrm{JS}}^{(t-1)})+\eta},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{MA}_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>MA</mtext><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{MA}_{w}</annotation></semantics></math> is length-<math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> moving average, <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta=10^{-3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta=10^{-3}</annotation></semantics></math> prevents division by zero. Binary flags trigger when ratios fall below thresholds for <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\text{stop}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>stop</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\text{stop}}</annotation></semantics></math> consecutive rounds:</p>
<table id="S3.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi_{I}^{(t)}=\mathbb{1}[r_{I}^{(t)}&lt;\varepsilon_{I}^{\text{rel}}],\quad\pi_{D}^{(t)}=\mathbb{1}[r_{D}^{(t)}&lt;\varepsilon_{D}^{\text{rel}}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>&lt;</mo><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mi>I</mi><mtext>rel</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>&lt;</mo><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mi>D</mi><mtext>rel</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{I}^{(t)}=\mathbb{1}[r_{I}^{(t)}&lt;\varepsilon_{I}^{\text{rel}}],\quad\pi_{D}^{(t)}=\mathbb{1}[r_{D}^{(t)}&lt;\varepsilon_{D}^{\text{rel}}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Behavior dial: scheduled contentiousness.</h5>

<div id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When plateaus detected, reduce contentiousness:</p>
<table id="S3.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CL}^{(t+1)}=[\mathrm{CL}^{(t)}-\alpha_{I}\pi_{I}^{(t)}-\alpha_{D}\pi_{D}^{(t)}]_{+}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>CL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>CL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CL}^{(t+1)}=[\mathrm{CL}^{(t)}-\alpha_{I}\pi_{I}^{(t)}-\alpha_{D}\pi_{D}^{(t)}]_{+}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">This transitions agents from exploratory (<math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CL}=0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>CL</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CL}=0.9</annotation></semantics></math>: “challenge aggressively”) to consolidative (<math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CL}=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>CL</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CL}=0.5</annotation></semantics></math>: “build on agreements”).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Information dial: raising evidence standards.</h5>

<div id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As consensus forms, admit increasingly higher-quality arguments:</p>
<table id="S3.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\tau}^{(t+1)}=\min\!\big\{\boldsymbol{\tau}^{(t)}+\gamma\,\pi_{I}^{(t)},\,\tau_{\max}\mathbf{1}\big\},~\boldsymbol{\tau}^{(t)}=\big(\tau_{\mathit{Q}}^{(t)},\,\tau_{\mathrm{CRIT}}^{(t)}\big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝝉</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.653em;" width="1.653em"><mi>min</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝝉</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>𝟏</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝝉</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>CRIT</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\tau}^{(t+1)}=\min\!\big\{\boldsymbol{\tau}^{(t)}+\gamma\,\pi_{I}^{(t)},\,\tau_{\max}\mathbf{1}\big\},~\boldsymbol{\tau}^{(t)}=\big(\tau_{\mathit{Q}}^{(t)},\,\tau_{\mathrm{CRIT}}^{(t)}\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the minimum is applied element-wise, and <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{1}\in\mathbb{R}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{1}\in\mathbb{R}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> is the all-ones vector for <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> gates (here <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m{=}2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m{=}2</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Stopping criterion.</h5>

<div id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Halt when both plateaus persist and evidence quality is sufficient:</p>
<table id="S3.E10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S3.E10X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E10X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{s=0}^{\tau_{\text{stop}}-1}\pi_{I}^{(t-s)}=\tau_{\text{stop}},~\sum_{s=0}^{\tau_{\text{stop}}-1}\pi_{D}^{(t-s)}=\tau_{\text{stop}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>stop</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>I</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>τ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>stop</mtext></msub><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>stop</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>D</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>τ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>stop</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{s=0}^{\tau_{\text{stop}}-1}\pi_{I}^{(t-s)}=\tau_{\text{stop}},~\sum_{s=0}^{\tau_{\text{stop}}-1}\pi_{D}^{(t-s)}=\tau_{\text{stop}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E10Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E10Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathit{Q}^{(t)}\geq\tau_{\mathit{Q}}^{(t)},\;\;\mathrm{O}^{(t)}\geq\tau_{\mathrm{O}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>≥</mo><mi>τ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>Q</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.727em">,</mo><mi>O</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>≥</mo><mi>τ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>O</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathit{Q}^{(t)}\geq\tau_{\mathit{Q}}^{(t)},\;\;\mathrm{O}^{(t)}\geq\tau_{\mathrm{O}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">This ensures that the gains have genuinely plateaued, not just temporarily stalled.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px6" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Learned scheduler (summary).</h5>

<div id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We replace the fixed <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\alpha,\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\alpha,\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math> schedule with a tiny bandit policy over a discrete action set of <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Delta\alpha,\Delta\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Delta\alpha,\Delta\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math> moves, optimizing per-round information gain and dispersion drop under a token budget. Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 1 (No-regret versus best fixed schedule). ‣ L.4 Main guarantee ‣ Appendix L Learned Scheduler for (𝛼,𝛾)" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> (Appx. <a href="#A12" title="Appendix L Learned Scheduler for (𝛼,𝛾)" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">L</span></a>) shows <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{O}(\sqrt{KT})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>O</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{O}(\sqrt{KT})</annotation></semantics></math> no-regret versus the best fixed schedule with zero expected budget violation.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px7" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Plateau guarantees (summary).</h5>

<div id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Under a gated averaging update with bounded noise, dispersion <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(t)</annotation></semantics></math> is non-increasing and the plateau controller terminates in <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(1/\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(1/\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> expected rounds. With a contraction condition the bound becomes <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\log(1/\varepsilon))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\log(1/\varepsilon))</annotation></semantics></math>. See Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 (Monotonicity under gated averaging). ‣ M.2 Monotonicity of dispersion ‣ Appendix M Plateau Guarantees" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition2" title="Proposition 2 (Termination in 𝑂(1/𝜀) expected rounds). ‣ M.4 Termination of the plateau controller ‣ Appendix M Plateau Guarantees" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> (Appx. <a href="#A13" title="Appendix M Plateau Guarantees" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">M</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px7.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px7.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px7.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">On dispersion.</em> Our guarantees analyze dispersion as the average <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px7.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{KL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>KL</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{KL}</annotation></semantics></math> to the running mixture, <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px7.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\mathrm{KL}}(t)=\frac{1}{m}\sum_{i}\mathrm{KL}(p_{t}^{(i)}\|\bar{p}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>m</mi></mfrac><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{KL}}(t)=\frac{1}{m}\sum_{i}\mathrm{KL}(p_{t}^{(i)}\|\bar{p}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, which yields monotonicity under gated averaging by convexity; in plots we additionally report <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px7.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{JSD}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>JSD</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{JSD}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is locally Lipschitz-equivalent on the <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px7.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>-smoothed simplex (Appx. <a href="#A13" title="Appendix M Plateau Guarantees" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">M</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.4 </span>Initialization Strategy</h3>

<div id="S3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Before debate, we compute initial evidence quality <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{Q}</annotation></semantics></math> and disagreement <math id="S3.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\mathrm{JS}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>JS</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{JS}}</annotation></semantics></math> from the query and retrieved context. We initialize contentiousness as</p>
<table id="S3.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CL}^{(1)}=\begin{cases}0.7&amp;\text{if }\mathit{Q}\geq\tau_{\mathit{Q}}^{\mathrm{hi}}\ \text{and}\ D_{\mathrm{JS}}\leq\tau_{D_{\mathrm{JS}}}^{\mathrm{lo}},\\[2.0pt]
0.9&amp;\text{if }\mathit{Q}\leq\tau_{\mathit{Q}}^{\mathrm{lo}}\ \text{and}\ D_{\mathrm{JS}}\geq\tau_{D_{\mathrm{JS}}}^{\mathrm{hi}},\\[2.0pt]
0.8&amp;\text{otherwise.}\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>CL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0.7</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>hi</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>and</mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>JS</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>JS</mi></msub><mi>lo</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0.9</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>lo</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>and</mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>JS</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>JS</mi></msub><mi>hi</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0.8</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext>otherwise.</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CL}^{(1)}=\begin{cases}0.7&amp;\text{if }\mathit{Q}\geq\tau_{\mathit{Q}}^{\mathrm{hi}}\ \text{and}\ D_{\mathrm{JS}}\leq\tau_{D_{\mathrm{JS}}}^{\mathrm{lo}},\\[2.0pt]
0.9&amp;\text{if }\mathit{Q}\leq\tau_{\mathit{Q}}^{\mathrm{lo}}\ \text{and}\ D_{\mathrm{JS}}\geq\tau_{D_{\mathrm{JS}}}^{\mathrm{hi}},\\[2.0pt]
0.8&amp;\text{otherwise.}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The thresholds <math id="S3.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\mathit{Q}}^{\mathrm{lo}},\tau_{\mathit{Q}}^{\mathrm{hi}},\tau_{D_{\mathrm{JS}}}^{\mathrm{lo}},\tau_{D_{\mathrm{JS}}}^{\mathrm{hi}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>lo</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>hi</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>JS</mi></msub><mi>lo</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>JS</mi></msub><mi>hi</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\mathit{Q}}^{\mathrm{lo}},\tau_{\mathit{Q}}^{\mathrm{hi}},\tau_{D_{\mathrm{JS}}}^{\mathrm{lo}},\tau_{D_{\mathrm{JS}}}^{\mathrm{hi}}</annotation></semantics></math> are set by percentiles on the development set (Appendix <a href="#A6" title="Appendix F Adaptive Initialization Strategy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F</span></a>). This reduces wasted exploration on straightforward cases while preserving search capacity on ambiguous ones.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.5 </span>Complete Algorithm</h3>

<div id="S3.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ Appendix C MACI Algorithm Specification" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> integrates all components (see Appx. <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C MACI Algorithm Specification" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a> for complete pseudocode).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.6 </span>Problem regime classification</h3>

<div id="S3.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S3.SS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MACI}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>MACI</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MACI}</annotation></semantics></math> targets open-ended reasoning where (1) the answer space is large (<math id="S3.SS6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{Y}|\geq 20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{Y}|\geq 20</annotation></semantics></math>), (2) evidence synthesis is required rather than pattern matching, and (3) uncertainty quantification matters. For small multiple-choice tasks (<math id="S3.SS6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{Y}|\leq 5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{Y}|\leq 5</annotation></semantics></math>), majority voting typically suffices. Appendix <a href="#A11.SS1" title="K.1 Problem regime formalization ‣ Appendix K Why Majority Voting Fails on Open-Ended Diagnosis" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">K.1</span></a> formalizes this distinction.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Empirical Validation</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate <math id="S4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MACI}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>MACI</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MACI}</annotation></semantics></math> in two domains, clinical diagnosis (G1) and news bias detection (G2), measuring accuracy, calibration, and cost, with ablations and case studies.</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1 </span>G1: Clinical Diagnosis</h3>

<section id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Dataset and protocol.</h5>

<div id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Kaggle Symptom–Disease</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tharmalingam, 2023</a>)</cite>: 1,500 cases across 30 diseases. The corpus provides only current symptoms (no labs or history). We use the <em id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">unconstrained</em> setting: models output free-text diagnoses from <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="100{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">100{+}</annotation></semantics></math> possibilities (no candidate list), matching clinical triage with broad differentials.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Why voting fails here.</h5>

<div id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When predictions are constrained to 30 labels, accuracy reaches 95–97%. In the unconstrained regime, agreement collapses and Acc@1 falls to 73–78% because many cases are under-specified and require evidence synthesis rather than pattern matching. Majority voting is unreliable in large output spaces (Appx. <a href="#A11" title="Appendix K Why Majority Voting Fails on Open-Ended Diagnosis" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">K</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Setup.</h5>

<div id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Backbones:</span> GPT-4o, Claude 3 Opus, Gemini 1.5 Pro; all pairs (<math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M{=}2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M{=}2</annotation></semantics></math>). <span id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Retrieval:</span> BM25 + dense reranking (<math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{\text{ret}}{=}32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mtext>ret</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{\text{ret}}{=}32</annotation></semantics></math>). <span id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Baselines:</span> best single; majority vote (20); self-consistency (20); fixed-contentiousness debate <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liang et al., 2024</a>)</cite>. <span id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Statistics:</span> BCa 95% CIs from <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B{=}20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B{=}20</annotation></semantics></math> bootstraps; paired Wilcoxon with Benjamini–Hochberg FDR (<math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q{=}0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q{=}0.05</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span>Pairwise <math id="S4.T2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MACI}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>MACI</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MACI}</annotation></semantics></math> vs. single models on 1,500 cases. Stars: paired Wilcoxon vs. best single (BH FDR <math id="S4.T2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q{=}0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q{=}0.05</annotation></semantics></math>): <math id="S4.T2.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}^{***}p{&lt;}0.001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∗</mo><mo lspace="0em">∗</mo></mrow></msup><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.001</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}^{***}p{&lt;}0.001</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.T2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{}^{**}p{&lt;}0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>p</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∗</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>∗</mo></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}^{**}p{&lt;}0.01</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
