</section>
<section id="S4.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">4.1.1 </span>Main Results, Three Parts</h4>

<section id="S4.SS1.SSS1.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Results #1: <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MACI}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>MACI</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MACI}</annotation></semantics></math> vs. single models.</h5>

<div id="S4.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Every <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MACI}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>MACI</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MACI}</annotation></semantics></math> pair outperforms its best single (Table <a href="#S4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ Setup. ‣ 4.1 G1: Clinical Diagnosis ‣ 4 Empirical Validation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>); for example, GPT–4o+Claude improves Acc@1 by +5.2 pp.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS1.SSS1.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Results #2: <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MACI}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>MACI</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MACI}</annotation></semantics></math> ablation.</h5>

<div id="S4.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MACI}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>MACI</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MACI}</annotation></semantics></math> relies on three active controls: (i) behavioral scheduling (high <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>CL</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CL}</annotation></semantics></math> for exploration, low <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>CL</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CL}</annotation></semantics></math> for consolidation),
(ii) <em id="S4.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">dual gating</em> (<math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q\geq\tau_{\text{Q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>Q</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q\geq\tau_{\text{Q}}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="S4.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">and</span> <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CRIT}\geq\tau_{\text{CRIT}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>CRIT</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>CRIT</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CRIT}\geq\tau_{\text{CRIT}}</annotation></semantics></math>),
and (iii) information–theoretic stopping (plateaus in <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\mathrm{JS}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>JS</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{JS}}</annotation></semantics></math> and IG). Fixed–contentiousness debate wastes tokens; passive aggregation uses 5–7<math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> more tokens and underperforms. Table <a href="#S4.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ Results #2: MACI ablation. ‣ 4.1.1 Main Results, Three Parts ‣ 4.1 G1: Clinical Diagnosis ‣ 4 Empirical Validation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> shows orthogonal effects: removing the <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{Q}</annotation></semantics></math> gate costs <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-5.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5.2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-5.2</annotation></semantics></math> pp Acc@1 and raises ECE by <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+0.040" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>0.040</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+0.040</annotation></semantics></math>; uniform weights (no reliability) cost <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-3.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-3.0</annotation></semantics></math> pp and <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+0.013" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>0.013</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+0.013</annotation></semantics></math> ECE; disabling scheduling (holding <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>CL</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CL}</annotation></semantics></math> high/low) costs <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-3.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-3.9</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.Px2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-6.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-6.0</annotation></semantics></math> pp with larger ECE.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 3: </span>Ablations on clinical diagnosis. <math id="S4.T3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> is the drop relative to full <math id="S4.T3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MACI}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>MACI</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MACI}</annotation></semantics></math> (lower is better). (Uniform weights = no reliability weighting)</figcaption>
<table id="S4.T3.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S4.T3.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T3.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;">Variant</th>
<th id="S4.T3.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;">Acc@1</th>
<th id="S4.T3.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><math id="S4.T3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math></th>
