</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="S4.F1.sf3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.04488v1/Fig_G1_CRIT_Improv.png" id="S4.F1.sf3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:673/142;" width="673" height="142" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(c) </span>Argument quality (<math id="S4.F1.sf3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CRIT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>CRIT</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CRIT}</annotation></semantics></math>) improves.</figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 1: </span>Internal signals over debate rounds (clinical). <span id="S4.F1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Left:</span> entropy declines under scheduled <math id="S4.F1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>CL</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CL}</annotation></semantics></math>.
<span id="S4.F1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Middle:</span> evidence quality <math id="S4.F1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{Q}</annotation></semantics></math> rises as the evidence gate <math id="S4.F1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\mathit{Q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\mathit{Q}}</annotation></semantics></math> tightens.
<span id="S4.F1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Right:</span> argument quality <math id="S4.F1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CRIT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>CRIT</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CRIT}</annotation></semantics></math> rises as low-quality arguments are filtered. Termination coincides with plateaued IG and low dispersion (not shown).</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS1.SSS1.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Results #3: <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.Px3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MACI}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>MACI</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MACI}</annotation></semantics></math> vs. competing schemes.</h5>

<div id="S4.SS1.SSS1.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS1.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Against debate/aggregation baselines, <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MACI}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>MACI</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MACI}</annotation></semantics></math> is more accurate and better calibrated with fewer tokens (Table <a href="#S4.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ Results #2: MACI ablation. ‣ 4.1.1 Main Results, Three Parts ‣ 4.1 G1: Clinical Diagnosis ‣ 4 Empirical Validation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>): +3.9 pp over majority vote and +3.7 pp over Liang et al. (both <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p{&lt;}0.001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.001</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p{&lt;}0.001</annotation></semantics></math>), ECE <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.081" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.081</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.081</annotation></semantics></math> vs. <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.103" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.103</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.103</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="19\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>19</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">19\%</annotation></semantics></math> fewer generation tokens. These gains align with the ablation evidence.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS1.SSS1.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Computational overhead.</h5>

<div id="S4.SS1.SSS1.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS1.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MACI}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>MACI</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MACI}</annotation></semantics></math> uses 18.4k tokens vs. 6.8k for a single model (2.7<math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> overhead). For high–stakes settings where accuracy reduces costly errors, this overhead is justified; for routine tasks, single–model inference may suffice.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS1.SSS1.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Evidence quality stratification.</h5>

<div id="S4.SS1.SSS1.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS1.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Accuracy correlates with initial <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{Q}</annotation></semantics></math>: cases with <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{Q}{&gt;}0.7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0.7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{Q}{&gt;}0.7</annotation></semantics></math> reach 78.3% vs. 69.8% for <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.Px5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{Q}{&lt;}0.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{Q}{&lt;}0.3</annotation></semantics></math> (Table 20, Appx. K). This validates <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.Px5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{Q}</annotation></semantics></math> as a useful signal and suggests retrieval improvements may benefit <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.Px5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MACI}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>MACI</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MACI}</annotation></semantics></math> more than parameter tuning.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS1.SSS1.Px6" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Controller guarantee (theory–lite).</h5>

<div id="S4.SS1.SSS1.Px6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS1.Px6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">With bounded noise and gated averaging, dispersion <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.Px6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(t)</annotation></semantics></math> is non–increasing, and the plateau controller terminates in <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.Px6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(1/\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(1/\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> expected rounds; under a contraction, <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.Px6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(t)</annotation></semantics></math> decays geometrically and termination is <math id="S4.SS1.SSS1.Px6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\log(1/\varepsilon))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\log(1/\varepsilon))</annotation></semantics></math> (Lem. <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 (Monotonicity under gated averaging). ‣ M.2 Monotonicity of dispersion ‣ Appendix M Plateau Guarantees" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, Prop. <a href="#Thmproposition2" title="Proposition 2 (Termination in 𝑂(1/𝜀) expected rounds). ‣ M.4 Termination of the plateau controller ‣ Appendix M Plateau Guarantees" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, Cor. <a href="#Thmcorollary1" title="Corollary 1 (Geometric contraction yields 𝑂(log(1/𝜀))). ‣ M.5 Contraction case ‣ Appendix M Plateau Guarantees" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, Appx. <a href="#A13" title="Appendix M Plateau Guarantees" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">M</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS1.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">4.1.2 </span>Two Case Studies: Active Control and Information Acquisition</h4>

<div id="S4.SS1.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We illustrate <math id="S4.SS1.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MACI}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>MACI</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MACI}</annotation></semantics></math>’s scheduling and gating, and show termination aligns with plateaued IG and low dispersion. Each case ends with a targeted information–acquisition plan specifying <em id="S4.SS1.SSS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">what to fetch next</em> for retrieval–augmented generation. Full transcripts appear in Appx. <a href="#A7" title="Appendix G Detailed MACI Case Study: Dengue vs. Chikungunya Diagnosis" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G</span></a> and <a href="#A8" title="Appendix H Extended MACI Case Study #2: Hepatitis Differential Diagnosis" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">H</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Case 1: Dengue vs. Chikungunya (3 rounds).</h5>

<div id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Symptoms:</span> skin rash, joint pain, vomiting, fatigue, high fever, headache, retro–orbital pain, myalgia, red spots. <span id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ground truth:</span> Dengue Fever.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S4.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ Case 1: Dengue vs. Chikungunya (3 rounds). ‣ 4.1.2 Two Case Studies: Active Control and Information Acquisition ‣ 4.1 G1: Clinical Diagnosis ‣ 4 Empirical Validation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> shows scheduling <math id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CL}\in\{0.9,0.7,0.5\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>CL</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0.9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CL}\in\{0.9,0.7,0.5\}</annotation></semantics></math>. <em id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">R1</em> (<math id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CL}{=}0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>CL</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CL}{=}0.9</annotation></semantics></math>): GPT–4o proposes specific viral diagnoses (Dengue 60%, Chikungunya 25%, Zika 15%); Gemini stays categorical (Viral Infection 60%, Autoimmune 20%, Bacterial 15%). High disagreement (<math id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\mathrm{JS}}{=}0.56" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>JS</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.56</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{JS}}{=}0.56</annotation></semantics></math>). <em id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">R2</em> (<math id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CL}{=}0.7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>CL</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CL}{=}0.7</annotation></semantics></math>): targeted challenges shift Gemini to Dengue (50%) and Chikungunya (30%); <math id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\mathrm{JS}}{=}0.37" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>JS</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.37</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{JS}}{=}0.37</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CRIT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>CRIT</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CRIT}</annotation></semantics></math> 0.75 <math id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> 0.82. <em id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">R3</em> (<math id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CL}{=}0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>CL</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CL}{=}0.5</annotation></semantics></math>): distributions align (Dengue 60%, Chikungunya 35%, Zika 5%); <math id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\mathrm{JS}}{=}0.02" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>JS</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.02</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{JS}}{=}0.02</annotation></semantics></math>, MI plateaus (0.49); trigger stop flags.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T5" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 5: </span>Signal evolution on a Dengue case. <math id="S4.T5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{W}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{W}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>: Wasserstein-1 distance; <math id="S4.T5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MI}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>MI</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MI}</annotation></semantics></math>: mutual information; <math id="S4.T5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\mathrm{JS}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>JS</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{JS}}</annotation></semantics></math>: Jensen–Shannon divergence. Lower is better for <math id="S4.T5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{W}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{W}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.T5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\mathrm{JS}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>JS</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{JS}}</annotation></semantics></math>; higher is better for <math id="S4.T5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MI}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>MI</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MI}</annotation></semantics></math>. (Appx <a href="#A4" title="Appendix D Information-Theoretic Signals for Debate Evaluation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a>)</figcaption>
<table id="S4.T5.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S4.T5.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T5.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T5.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Round</span></th>
<td id="S4.T5.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><math id="S4.T5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\mathrm{CL}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐂𝐋</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\mathrm{CL}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S4.T5.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><math id="S4.T5.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\widetilde{W}}_{\boldsymbol{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑾</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>𝟏</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\widetilde{W}}_{\boldsymbol{1}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S4.T5.2.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><math id="S4.T5.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\mathrm{MI}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐌𝐈</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\mathrm{MI}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S4.T5.2.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><math id="S4.T5.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{D_{\mathrm{JS}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑫</mi><mi>𝐉𝐒</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{D_{\mathrm{JS}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T5.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T5.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">1</th>
<td id="S4.T5.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">0.9</td>
<td id="S4.T5.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">0.68</td>
<td id="S4.T5.2.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">0.43</td>
<td id="S4.T5.2.2.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">0.56</td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T5.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T5.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">2</th>
<td id="S4.T5.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.7</td>
<td id="S4.T5.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.44</td>
<td id="S4.T5.2.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.46</td>
<td id="S4.T5.2.3.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.37</td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T5.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T5.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">3</th>
<td id="S4.T5.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.5</td>
<td id="S4.T5.2.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.36</td>
<td id="S4.T5.2.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.49</td>
<td id="S4.T5.2.4.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.02</td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T5.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T5.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t" colspan="2"><span id="S4.T5.2.5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Change (R1 <math id="S4.T5.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\to" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\to</annotation></semantics></math> R3)</span></th>
<td id="S4.T5.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><math id="S4.T5.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-47\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>47</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-47\%</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S4.T5.2.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><math id="S4.T5.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+14\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>14</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+14\%</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S4.T5.2.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><math id="S4.T5.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-96\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>96</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-96\%</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Figure 1 (internal signals).</h5>

<div id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fig. <a href="#S4.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ Results #2: MACI ablation. ‣ 4.1.1 Main Results, Three Parts ‣ 4.1 G1: Clinical Diagnosis ‣ 4 Empirical Validation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> shows entropy declining as <math id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>CL</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CL}</annotation></semantics></math> moves from explore to consolidate; <math id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{Q}</annotation></semantics></math> rising as the gate <math id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> tightens; and <math id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CRIT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>CRIT</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CRIT}</annotation></semantics></math> increasing as low–quality arguments are filtered. Dispersion <math id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\mathrm{JS}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>JS</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{JS}}</annotation></semantics></math> (not shown) falls in parallel; termination matches IG and dispersion plateaus.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Evaluator robustness.</h5>

<div id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Reversing debater order leaves the <math id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CRIT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>CRIT</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CRIT}</annotation></semantics></math> winner unchanged; cross–family judge swaps preserve item–level rankings (Appx. <a href="#A5.SS7" title="E.7 CRIT Reliability and Role in MACI ‣ Appendix E CRIT: Cross-Family Argument Quality Evaluator" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.7</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Informative RAG recommendations.</h5>

<div id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Beyond “Dengue Fever (60%),” <math id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MACI}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>MACI</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MACI}</annotation></semantics></math> outputs a plan: <em id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Questions</em> (endemic travel; bleeding/bruising), <em id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Labs</em> (CBC for thrombocytopenia; IgM/IgG; PCR; NS1 antigen), plus retrieval cues for RAG.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Case 2: Hepatitis differential (4 rounds, adaptive stopping).</h5>

<div id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Symptoms:</span> itching, vomiting, fatigue, weight loss, high fever, jaundice, dark urine, abdominal pain. <span id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ground truth:</span> Hepatitis C.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.F2" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2"><img src="2510.04488v1/FigureDenguFever.jpg" id="S4.F2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:317/153;" width="317" height="153" alt="Refer to caption"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2"><img src="2510.04488v1/Figure-Hapititas.jpg" id="S4.F2.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:317/161;" width="317" height="161" alt="Refer to caption"></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 2: </span>Convergence in two cases: <math id="S4.F2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\mathrm{JS}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>JS</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{JS}}</annotation></semantics></math> and allied distances decrease monotonically under scheduling.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S4.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ Case 2: Hepatitis differential (4 rounds, adaptive stopping). ‣ 4.1.2 Two Case Studies: Active Control and Information Acquisition ‣ 4.1 G1: Clinical Diagnosis ‣ 4 Empirical Validation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> shows <math id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CL}\in\{0.9,0.7,0.5,0.3\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>CL</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0.9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CL}\in\{0.9,0.7,0.5,0.3\}</annotation></semantics></math>. <em id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">R1</em> (<math id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CL}{=}0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>CL</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CL}{=}0.9</annotation></semantics></math>): GPT–4o emphasizes HCV (40%); Claude emphasizes HBV (35%) and alcoholic hepatitis (15%); <math id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\mathrm{JS}}{=}0.22" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>JS</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.22</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{JS}}{=}0.22</annotation></semantics></math>. <em id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px5.p2.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">R2</em> (<math id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CL}{=}0.7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>CL</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CL}{=}0.7</annotation></semantics></math>): reasoning integration; <math id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\mathrm{JS}}{=}0.12" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>JS</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.12</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{JS}}{=}0.12</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px5.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CRIT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>CRIT</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CRIT}</annotation></semantics></math> rises. <em id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px5.p2.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">R3</em> (<math id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px5.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CL}{=}0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>CL</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CL}{=}0.5</annotation></semantics></math>): near convergence (HCV 35%, HBV 25–30%, cirrhosis 20%); <math id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px5.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\mathrm{JS}}{=}0.04" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>JS</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.04</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{JS}}{=}0.04</annotation></semantics></math>, MI 0.49. <em id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px5.p2.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">R4</em> (<math id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px5.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CL}{=}0.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>CL</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CL}{=}0.3</annotation></semantics></math>): distributions nearly identical; termination.</p>
</div>
