<section id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px6" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Internal signals (case view).</h5>

<div id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As in Case 1, entropy declines as <math id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>CL</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CL}</annotation></semantics></math> schedules down; <math id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{Q}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CRIT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>CRIT</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CRIT}</annotation></semantics></math> rise with tighter gates; <math id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\mathrm{JS}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>JS</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{JS}}</annotation></semantics></math> falls toward zero. Fig. <a href="#S4.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ Case 2: Hepatitis differential (4 rounds, adaptive stopping). ‣ 4.1.2 Two Case Studies: Active Control and Information Acquisition ‣ 4.1 G1: Clinical Diagnosis ‣ 4 Empirical Validation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> visualizes monotonic dispersion declines for both cases.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px7" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Evaluator robustness.</h5>

<div id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The same checks apply: order swap and cross–family judge swap leave outcomes stable (Appx. <a href="#A5.SS7" title="E.7 CRIT Reliability and Role in MACI ‣ Appendix E CRIT: Cross-Family Argument Quality Evaluator" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.7</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px8" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Informative RAG recommendations.</h5>

<div id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px8.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MACI}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>MACI</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MACI}</annotation></semantics></math> outputs: <em id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Labs</em> (HAV/HBV/HCV serology; LFTs ALT/AST/bilirubin/alkaline phosphatase; CBC; INR), <em id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px8.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Imaging</em> (abdominal ultrasound), <em id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px8.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">History</em> (alcohol/medications, injection drug use, transfusions), <em id="S4.SS1.SSS2.Px8.p1.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Monitoring</em> (encephalopathy, coagulopathy).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2 </span>G2: News Bias Detection (Cross–Domain)</h3>

<section id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Why this tests portability.</h5>

<div id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">News bias differs from G1 on <em id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">evidence</em> (full articles vs. symptom lists), <em id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">labels</em> (5–point continuous vs. discrete), and <em id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">ground truth</em> (partisan–anchored vs. objective). A self–supervised study maps <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>CL</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CL}</annotation></semantics></math> to linguistic patterns across topics (Table <a href="#A9.T15" title="Table 15 ‣ Appendix I Mapping Between Contentiousness Intensity and Linguistic Characteristics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>, Appx. <a href="#A9" title="Appendix I Mapping Between Contentiousness Intensity and Linguistic Characteristics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">I</span></a>): high <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CL}{=}0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>CL</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CL}{=}0.9</annotation></semantics></math> is confrontational, low <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CL}{=}0.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>CL</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CL}{=}0.3</annotation></semantics></math> is cooperative. A shallow classifier predicts <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>CL</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CL}</annotation></semantics></math> bins with AUC <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.83" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.83</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.83</annotation></semantics></math> (Table <a href="#A9.T17" title="Table 17 ‣ Manipulation check. ‣ Appendix I Mapping Between Contentiousness Intensity and Linguistic Characteristics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>), indicating measurable behavior modulation beyond domain content.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Dataset and setup.</h5>

<div id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use 619 scandal articles from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Budak et al., 2016</a>)</cite> with Democrat/Republican five–point ratings (<math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-2</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+2</annotation></semantics></math>). Hyperparameters match G1: <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CL}\in\{0.9,0.7,0.5\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>CL</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0.9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CL}\in\{0.9,0.7,0.5\}</annotation></semantics></math>, gates (<math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\mathit{Q}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\mathit{Q}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\mathrm{O}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>O</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\mathrm{O}}</annotation></semantics></math>), and the same stopping rule. Two agents (GPT–4o, Claude 3 Opus) start with asymmetric partisan framings.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T7" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 7: </span>News bias results (619 articles). <em id="S4.T7.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Tokens are reported in thousands</em> (<math id="S4.T7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times 10^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times 10^{3}</annotation></semantics></math>). MAD: mean absolute deviation from centrist (0).</figcaption>
<table id="S4.T7.4" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S4.T7.4.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T7.4.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;">Method</th>
<th id="S4.T7.4.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;">MAD</th>
<th id="S4.T7.4.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;">ECE</th>
<th id="S4.T7.4.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;">Brier</th>
<th id="S4.T7.4.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;">Tokens</th>
<th id="S4.T7.4.1.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;">Rounds</th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S4.T7.4.2" class="ltx_tr">
