</section>
<section id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Results #1: Narrowing partisan gaps.</h5>

<div id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Partisan annotators diverge (MAD 0.84 vs. 0.76). Averaging yields 0.51; unscheduled debate 0.38. <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MACI}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>MACI</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MACI}</annotation></semantics></math> achieves <span id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.12</span> MAD (<span id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">76%</span> vs. averaging, <span id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">68%</span> vs. unscheduled), with better calibration (ECE 0.093 vs. 0.127–0.173) and <span id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">30%</span> fewer tokens (8.2 vs. 11.7). Fig. <a href="#S4.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ Results #3: Signal convergence and behavioral transfer. ‣ 4.2 G2: News Bias Detection (Cross–Domain) ‣ 4 Empirical Validation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>a shows centering between partisan peaks.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Results #2: Which controls matter (ablations).</h5>

<div id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Removing scheduling raises MAD by +0.14–0.19; removing the <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{Q}</annotation></semantics></math> gate by +0.17; uniform (no–reliability) weights by +0.06 and ECE by +0.014 (Table <a href="#S4.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ Results #2: Which controls matter (ablations). ‣ 4.2 G2: News Bias Detection (Cross–Domain) ‣ 4 Empirical Validation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T8" class="ltx_table">
