<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Configuration and Hyperparameters</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Default Hyperparameters</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Unless specified otherwise, <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MACI}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>MACI</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MACI}</annotation></semantics></math> uses these settings across all experiments:</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Control parameters.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="A2.I1" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.2em;">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Reliability smoothing (EMA):</span> <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=0.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=0.8</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=10^{-6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=10^{-6}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Initial gates:</span> <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\mathit{Q}}^{(1)}=0.50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>0.50</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\mathit{Q}}^{(1)}=0.50</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\mathrm{CRIT}}^{(1)}=0.30" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>CRIT</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>0.30</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\mathrm{CRIT}}^{(1)}=0.30</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Gate tightening:</span> <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\tau_{\mathit{Q}}^{(t+1)},\tau_{\mathrm{CRIT}}^{(t+1)})\leftarrow\min\!\big\{(\tau_{\mathit{Q}}^{(t)},\tau_{\mathrm{CRIT}}^{(t)})+\gamma\,\pi_{I}^{(t)},\,(\tau_{\max},\tau_{\max})\big\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>CRIT</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.653em;" width="1.653em"><mi>min</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>CRIT</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tau_{\mathit{Q}}^{(t+1)},\tau_{\mathrm{CRIT}}^{(t+1)})\leftarrow\min\!\big\{(\tau_{\mathit{Q}}^{(t)},\tau_{\mathrm{CRIT}}^{(t)})+\gamma\,\pi_{I}^{(t)},\,(\tau_{\max},\tau_{\max})\big\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Overlap floor for stopping (not an admission gate):</span> <math id="A2.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\mathrm{O}}=0.30" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>O</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.30</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\mathrm{O}}=0.30</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Initialization bins (development set).</h5>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="A2.I2" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.2em;">
<li id="A2.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">High quality (<math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{Q}\geq 0.7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0.7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{Q}\geq 0.7</annotation></semantics></math>) and low disagreement (<math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\mathrm{JS}}\leq 0.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>JS</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>0.3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{JS}}\leq 0.3</annotation></semantics></math>): <math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CL}^{(1)}=0.7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>CL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0.7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CL}^{(1)}=0.7</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Low quality (<math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{Q}\leq 0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{Q}\leq 0.5</annotation></semantics></math>) and high disagreement (<math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\mathrm{JS}}\geq 0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>JS</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{JS}}\geq 0.5</annotation></semantics></math>): <math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CL}^{(1)}=0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>CL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CL}^{(1)}=0.9</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Otherwise: <math id="A2.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CL}^{(1)}=0.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>CL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0.8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CL}^{(1)}=0.8</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Contentiousness schedule.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Standard progression: <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CL}\in\{0.9,0.7,0.5,0.3\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>CL</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0.9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CL}\in\{0.9,0.7,0.5,0.3\}</annotation></semantics></math> with adaptive transitions triggered by plateau flags.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Clinical Diagnosis (G1) Setup</h3>

<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Dataset.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Kaggle Symptom-Disease Corpus, stratified split: 1,500 test cases (50 per disease, 30 conditions). Train/dev/test files and random seeds provided in supplement.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Retrieval.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">BM25 with dense reranker (all-MiniLM-L6-v2), <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{\text{ret}}=32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mtext>ret</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{\text{ret}}=32</annotation></semantics></math>, max context 4k tokens.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Backbones.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="A2.I3" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.2em;">
<li id="A2.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">GPT-4o (gpt-4o-2024-08-06)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Claude 3 Opus (claude-3-opus-20240229)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Gemini 1.5 Pro (gemini-1.5-pro-001)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I3.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I3.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I3.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Temperature: 0.7 for all agents</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Evaluation.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">20 bootstrap resamples for confidence intervals. BCa method. Paired Wilcoxon tests with Benjamini-Hochberg FDR correction at <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=0.05</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>News Bias (G2) Setup</h3>

<section id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Dataset.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">619 scandal-focused articles with partisan annotations (5-point scale). <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Budak et al., 2016</a>]</cite> collected 803,146 articles from fifteen U.S. news outlets,cidentifying 10,502 political articles. We focus on scandals as this content
exhibits the strongest partisan disagreement.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Agents.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">GPT-4o and Claude 3 Opus with asymmetric initialization (one Democrat-framed, one Republican-framed).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Identical hyperparameters.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Same <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>CL</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CL}</annotation></semantics></math> schedule, gates, stopping criteria as G1. No domain-specific tuning.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>MACI Algorithm Specification</h2>

<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> <math id="alg1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MACI}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>MACI</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MACI}</annotation></semantics></math> Moderator with Dual-Dial Control</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
            
            
           Initialize debate record <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi^{(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi^{(1)}</annotation></semantics></math>; set <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CL^{(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CL^{(1)}</annotation></semantics></math> via dev binning; set gates <math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\text{Q}}^{(1)}=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mtext>Q</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\text{Q}}^{(1)}=0.5</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\text{CRIT}}^{(1)}=0.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mtext>CRIT</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>0.3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\text{CRIT}}^{(1)}=0.3</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
            
            
           <span id="alg1.l2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1,2,\dots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1,2,\dots</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
            
            
            Provide <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{(t)}=\big(\psi^{(t)},\,CL^{(t)},\,\tau_{\text{Q}}^{(t)},\,\tau_{\text{CRIT}}^{(t)}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mtext>Q</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mtext>CRIT</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{(t)}=\big(\psi^{(t)},\,CL^{(t)},\,\tau_{\text{Q}}^{(t)},\,\tau_{\text{CRIT}}^{(t)}\big)</annotation></semantics></math> to both agents.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in\{A,B\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in\{A,B\}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
            
            
             Agent <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> emits claim–justification pairs, <math id="alg1.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{u}^{(t)}\in\Delta(\mathcal{Y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{u}^{(t)}\in\Delta(\mathcal{Y})</annotation></semantics></math>, cites <math id="alg1.l5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathcal{E}}_{u}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathcal{E}}_{u}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Admission (dual gate).</span> For each candidate argument <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> from either agent, compute a per-argument evidence score <math id="alg1.l7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> (analogous to Eq. (<a href="#S3.E1" title="Equation 1 ‣ Signal 1: Evidence quality (𝑄). ‣ 3.2 Four Measurement Signals ‣ 3 MACI: Information and Behavior Dials with Measurable Stopping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>), using only spans cited by <math id="alg1.l7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>) and its <math id="alg1.l7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CRIT}_{i}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>CRIT</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CRIT}_{i}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
            
            
            Admit <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> into <math id="alg1.l8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi^{(t+1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi^{(t+1)}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">iff</span> <math id="alg1.l8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}^{(t)}\geq\tau_{\text{Q}}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>≥</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mtext>Q</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}^{(t)}\geq\tau_{\text{Q}}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">and</span> <math id="alg1.l8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CRIT}_{i}^{(t)}\geq\tau_{\text{CRIT}}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>CRIT</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>≥</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mtext>CRIT</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CRIT}_{i}^{(t)}\geq\tau_{\text{CRIT}}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>; otherwise discard.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
            
            
            Update reliability: <math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma_{u}^{(t)}\leftarrow\lambda\,\Gamma_{u}^{(t-1)}+(1-\lambda)\,\overline{\mathrm{CRIT}}_{u,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>CRIT</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma_{u}^{(t)}\leftarrow\lambda\,\Gamma_{u}^{(t-1)}+(1-\lambda)\,\overline{\mathrm{CRIT}}_{u,t}</annotation></semantics></math>; compute <math id="alg1.l9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{u}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{u}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> via Eq. (<a href="#S3.E4" title="Equation 4 ‣ Signal 4: Argument quality (CRIT). ‣ 3.2 Four Measurement Signals ‣ 3 MACI: Information and Behavior Dials with Measurable Stopping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>).

</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
            
            
            Form mixture: <math id="alg1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{(t)}=\sum_{u}\omega_{u}^{(t)}p_{u}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>u</mi></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{(t)}=\sum_{u}\omega_{u}^{(t)}p_{u}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>; compute <math id="alg1.l10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{I}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{I}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> via Eq. (<a href="#S3.E5" title="Equation 5 ‣ Information gain. ‣ 3.3 Dual-Dial Control with Plateau Detection ‣ 3 MACI: Information and Behavior Dials with Measurable Stopping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>).

</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">11:</span>
            
            
            Compute signals: <math id="alg1.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\mathrm{JS}}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>JS</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{JS}}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> (Eq. <a href="#S3.E2" title="Equation 2 ‣ Signal 2: Disagreement (𝐷_JS). ‣ 3.2 Four Measurement Signals ‣ 3 MACI: Information and Behavior Dials with Measurable Stopping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>), <math id="alg1.l11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{O}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{O}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> (Eq. <a href="#S3.E3" title="Equation 3 ‣ Signal 3: Support overlap (O). ‣ 3.2 Four Measurement Signals ‣ 3 MACI: Information and Behavior Dials with Measurable Stopping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>), <math id="alg1.l11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{Q}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{Q}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> (Eq. <a href="#S3.E1" title="Equation 1 ‣ Signal 1: Evidence quality (𝑄). ‣ 3.2 Four Measurement Signals ‣ 3 MACI: Information and Behavior Dials with Measurable Stopping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>).

</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">12:</span>
            
            
            Update progress ratios <math id="alg1.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{I}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{I}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{D}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{D}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> and flags <math id="alg1.l12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{I}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{I}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{D}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{D}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> via Eqs. (<a href="#S3.E6" title="Equation 6 ‣ Plateau detection via relative progress ratios. ‣ 3.3 Dual-Dial Control with Plateau Detection ‣ 3 MACI: Information and Behavior Dials with Measurable Stopping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>)–(<a href="#S3.E7" title="Equation 7 ‣ Plateau detection via relative progress ratios. ‣ 3.3 Dual-Dial Control with Plateau Detection ‣ 3 MACI: Information and Behavior Dials with Measurable Stopping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>).

</div>
<div id="alg1.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">13:</span>
            
            
            Update dials: <math id="alg1.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CL^{(t+1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CL^{(t+1)}</annotation></semantics></math> via Eq. (<a href="#S3.E8" title="Equation 8 ‣ Behavior dial: scheduled contentiousness. ‣ 3.3 Dual-Dial Control with Plateau Detection ‣ 3 MACI: Information and Behavior Dials with Measurable Stopping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>); apply Eq. (<a href="#S3.E9" title="Equation 9 ‣ Information dial: raising evidence standards. ‣ 3.3 Dual-Dial Control with Plateau Detection ‣ 3 MACI: Information and Behavior Dials with Measurable Stopping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>) <em id="alg1.l13.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">componentwise</em> to obtain <math id="alg1.l13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\tau_{\text{Q}}^{(t+1)},\,\tau_{\text{CRIT}}^{(t+1)}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mtext>Q</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mtext>CRIT</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\tau_{\text{Q}}^{(t+1)},\,\tau_{\text{CRIT}}^{(t+1)}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">14:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> stopping criterion Eq. (<a href="#S3.E10" title="Equation 10 ‣ Stopping criterion. ‣ 3.3 Dual-Dial Control with Plateau Detection ‣ 3 MACI: Information and Behavior Dials with Measurable Stopping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>) satisfied <span id="alg1.l14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">15:</span>
            
            
             <span id="alg1.l15.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> calibrated <math id="alg1.l15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> and curated debate record <math id="alg1.l15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">16:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l16.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">17:</span>
            
            
           <span id="alg1.l17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Default hyperparameters: <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w{=}3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w{=}3</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta{=}10^{-3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta{=}10^{-3}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda{=}0.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda{=}0.8</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon{=}10^{-6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon{=}10^{-6}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\text{stop}}{=}2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>stop</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\text{stop}}{=}2</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{I}{=}\alpha_{D}{=}0.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{I}{=}\alpha_{D}{=}0.2</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma{=}0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma{=}0.1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\text{Q}}^{(1)}{=}0.50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mtext>Q</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>0.50</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\text{Q}}^{(1)}{=}0.50</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\text{CRIT}}^{(1)}{=}0.30" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mtext>CRIT</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>0.30</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\text{CRIT}}^{(1)}{=}0.30</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Information-Theoretic Signals for Debate Evaluation</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This appendix presents the mathematical foundations underlying MACI’s measurement and control framework. We detail each metric’s properties, computational requirements, and specific role in debate moderation.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Target prototype construction <math id="A4.SS1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Metric Selection and Usage in MACI</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We highlight each metric’s properties and how MACI employs them in practice:</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ol id="A4.I1" class="ltx_enumerate" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.2em;">
<li id="A4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Cross-Entropy (CE).</span>
Likelihood surrogate that mixes uncertainty and mismatch <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shore and Johnson, 1980</a>, <a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cover and Thomas, 2006</a>]</cite>. <em id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">MACI use:</em> reporting and ablation studies, calibration assessment—not a primary control signal due to asymmetry and sensitivity to probability shifts.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Entropy.</span>
Quantifies uncertainty in a single prediction <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shannon, 1948</a>]</cite>. <em id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">MACI use:</em> per-round <em id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">information gain</em> via normalized entropy reduction of the reliability-weighted aggregate.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Kullback–Leibler (KL) divergence.</span>
Directed discrepancy measure that is asymmetric and support-sensitive <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kullback, 1951</a>, <a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cover and Thomas, 2006</a>]</cite>. <em id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">MACI use:</em> auxiliary analysis to detect directional belief shifts; not the primary disagreement metric due to asymmetry concerns in symmetric debate settings.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Jensen–Shannon (<math id="A4.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\mathrm{JS}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>JS</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{JS}}</annotation></semantics></math>) divergence.</span>
Symmetric, bounded [0,1], and finite even under disjoint support; <math id="A4.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{D_{\mathrm{JS}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>JS</mi></msub></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{D_{\mathrm{JS}}}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies triangle inequality, forming a true metric <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lin, 1991</a>]</cite>. <em id="A4.I1.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">MACI use:</em> primary <em id="A4.I1.i4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">disagreement</em> signal for discrete labels via unified distance measure <math id="A4.I1.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">5.</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mutual Information (MI) and Normalized MI.</span>
Measures shared information between random variables <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cover and Thomas, 2006</a>]</cite>; text-based MI estimators can exhibit high variance. <em id="A4.I1.i5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">MACI use:</em> logged for analysis and visualization; excluded from control loop due to estimation instability.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">6.</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I1.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Wasserstein Distance (WD).</span>
Geometry-aware discrepancy that respects label structure; efficiently computable in 1D via cumulative distribution functions <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kantorovich, 1942</a>]</cite>. <em id="A4.I1.i6.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">MACI use:</em> disagreement measurement for ordered or structured outputs via unified distance measure <math id="A4.I1.i6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i7" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">7.</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Information Gain (IG).</span>
Entropy reduction of the reliability-weighted mixture, normalized by <math id="A4.I1.i7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log|\mathcal{Y}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log|\mathcal{Y}|</annotation></semantics></math> for interpretability <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cover and Thomas, 2006</a>]</cite>. <em id="A4.I1.i7.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">MACI use:</em> primary convergence signal with moving average plateau detection.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3 </span>Integration in MACI Framework</h3>

<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">MACI employs these signals in three distinct capacities:</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Primary Control Signals.</h5>

<div id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The unified distance measure <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> adapts to output type: <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{(t)}:=D_{\mathrm{JS}}(\{B_{i}^{(t)}\})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>JS</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{(t)}:=D_{\mathrm{JS}}(\{B_{i}^{(t)}\})</annotation></semantics></math> for categorical labels and <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{(t)}:=\widetilde{W}_{1}(\{B_{i}^{(t)}\})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{(t)}:=\widetilde{W}_{1}(\{B_{i}^{(t)}\})</annotation></semantics></math> for structured outputs. This provides consistent plateau detection logic while respecting task-appropriate geometry.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Progress Tracking.</h5>

<div id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Normalized information gain <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{I}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{I}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> with moving average <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MA}_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>MA</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MA}_{w}</annotation></semantics></math> quantifies uncertainty resolution. Plateau detection (<math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\widehat{I}^{(t)}&lt;\varepsilon_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\widehat{I}^{(t)}&lt;\varepsilon_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\text{stop}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>stop</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\text{stop}}</annotation></semantics></math> rounds) triggers contentiousness reduction: <math id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CL}^{(t+1)}=[\mathrm{CL}^{(t)}-\alpha_{I}]_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>CL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>CL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CL}^{(t+1)}=[\mathrm{CL}^{(t)}-\alpha_{I}]_{+}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Analysis and Validation.</h5>

<div id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">KL divergence reveals directional bias in agent updates. Mutual information tracks shared representational structure. Cross-entropy supports calibration assessment. These signals inform post-hoc analysis but don’t participate in real-time control.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.4 </span>Mathematical Formulations</h3>

<section id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Normalized Information Gain</h5>

<div id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A4.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{I}^{(t)}:=\frac{H(p^{(t-1)})-H(p^{(t)})}{\log|\mathcal{Y}|},\quad p^{(t)}=\sum_{u}\omega_{u}^{(t)}p_{u}^{(t)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>u</mi></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{I}^{(t)}:=\frac{H(p^{(t-1)})-H(p^{(t)})}{\log|\mathcal{Y}|},\quad p^{(t)}=\sum_{u}\omega_{u}^{(t)}p_{u}^{(t)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Moving Average Plateau Detection</h5>

<div id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A4.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\widehat{I}^{(t)}:=\mathrm{MA}_{w}(\widehat{I}^{(t)})-\mathrm{MA}_{w}(\widehat{I}^{(t-1)})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>MA</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>MA</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\widehat{I}^{(t)}:=\mathrm{MA}_{w}(\widehat{I}^{(t)})-\mathrm{MA}_{w}(\widehat{I}^{(t-1)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MA}_{w}(x^{(t)})=\frac{1}{w}\sum_{i=0}^{w-1}x^{(t-i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>MA</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>w</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MA}_{w}(x^{(t)})=\frac{1}{w}\sum_{i=0}^{w-1}x^{(t-i)}</annotation></semantics></math> is the length-<math id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> moving average.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Jensen-Shannon Divergence</h5>

<div id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A4.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\mathrm{JS}}(P,Q)=\frac{1}{2}D_{KL}(P\|M)+\frac{1}{2}D_{KL}(Q\|M)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>JS</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{JS}}(P,Q)=\frac{1}{2}D_{KL}(P\|M)+\frac{1}{2}D_{KL}(Q\|M),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A4.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=\frac{1}{2}(P+Q)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=\frac{1}{2}(P+Q).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Normalized Wasserstein Distance</h5>

<div id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For cumulative distribution functions <math id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{P}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{Q}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{W}_{1}(P,Q)=\frac{W_{1}(P,Q)}{\max_{P^{\prime},Q^{\prime}}W_{1}(P^{\prime},Q^{\prime})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{W}_{1}(P,Q)=\frac{W_{1}(P,Q)}{\max_{P^{\prime},Q^{\prime}}W_{1}(P^{\prime},Q^{\prime})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Unified Distance Measure</h5>

<div id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A4.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{(t)}=\begin{cases}D_{\mathrm{JS}}(\{B_{i}^{(t)}\}_{i=1}^{M})&amp;\text{categorical labels}\\
\widetilde{W}_{1}(\{B_{i}^{(t)}\}_{i=1}^{M})&amp;\text{structured labels}\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>JS</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext>categorical labels</mtext></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext>structured labels</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{(t)}=\begin{cases}D_{\mathrm{JS}}(\{B_{i}^{(t)}\}_{i=1}^{M})&amp;\text{categorical labels}\\
\widetilde{W}_{1}(\{B_{i}^{(t)}\}_{i=1}^{M})&amp;\text{structured labels}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.5 </span>Control Logic and Termination</h3>

<section id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Contentiousness Reduction.</h5>

<div id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Define <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[x]_{+}:=\max(0,x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[x]_{+}:=\max(0,x)</annotation></semantics></math>. Two plateau monitors trigger intensity reduction:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\text{IG plateau:}\quad\Delta\widehat{I}^{(t)}&lt;\varepsilon_{I}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>IG plateau:</mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>I</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{IG plateau:}\quad\Delta\widehat{I}^{(t)}&lt;\varepsilon_{I}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A4.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{for }\tau_{\text{stop}}\text{ rounds}\Rightarrow\mathrm{CL}^{(t+1)}=[\mathrm{CL}^{(t)}-\alpha_{I}]_{+}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>stop</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> rounds</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><msup><mi>CL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>CL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{for }\tau_{\text{stop}}\text{ rounds}\Rightarrow\mathrm{CL}^{(t+1)}=[\mathrm{CL}^{(t)}-\alpha_{I}]_{+}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A4.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\text{Dispersion plateau:}\quad|D^{(t)}-D^{(t-1)}|&lt;\varepsilon_{D}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Dispersion plateau:</mtext><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>D</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>D</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Dispersion plateau:}\quad|D^{(t)}-D^{(t-1)}|&lt;\varepsilon_{D}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A4.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{for }\tau_{\text{stop}}\text{ rounds}\Rightarrow\mathrm{CL}^{(t+1)}=[\mathrm{CL}^{(t)}-\alpha_{D}]_{+}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>stop</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> rounds</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><msup><mi>CL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>CL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{for }\tau_{\text{stop}}\text{ rounds}\Rightarrow\mathrm{CL}^{(t+1)}=[\mathrm{CL}^{(t)}-\alpha_{D}]_{+}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Termination Criteria.</h5>

<div id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Debate stops when the Eq. (10) plateau conditions hold (for <math id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\text{stop}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>stop</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\text{stop}}</annotation></semantics></math> rounds); we also stop early on budget exhaustion or sustained low CRIT (validator stalemate).</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="A4.I2" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.2em;">
<li id="A4.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">IG plateau: <math id="A4.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\widehat{I}^{(t)}&lt;\varepsilon_{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>I</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>I</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\widehat{I}^{(t)}&lt;\varepsilon_{I}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A4.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\text{stop}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>stop</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\text{stop}}</annotation></semantics></math> rounds</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Dispersion stabilization: <math id="A4.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|D^{(t)}-D^{(t-1)}|&lt;\varepsilon_{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|D^{(t)}-D^{(t-1)}|&lt;\varepsilon_{D}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A4.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\text{stop}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>stop</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\text{stop}}</annotation></semantics></math> rounds</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Budget exhaustion: token/time limits reached</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Validator stalemate: CRIT quality below threshold for extended period</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.6 </span>Practical Interpretation Guidelines</h3>

<section id="A4.SS6.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Typical Value Ranges and Decision Thresholds.</h5>

<div id="A4.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Based on empirical analysis across clinical reasoning and synthesis tasks:</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="A4.I3" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.2em;">
<li id="A4.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A4.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\mathrm{JS}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>JS</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{JS}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> values</span>: <math id="A4.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;0.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0.3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;0.3</annotation></semantics></math> indicates substantial disagreement warranting continued debate; <math id="A4.I3.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;0.1</annotation></semantics></math> suggests near-consensus</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Information Gain</span>: Normalized values <math id="A4.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;0.1</annotation></semantics></math> indicate meaningful uncertainty reduction; <math id="A4.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;0.02" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.02</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;0.02</annotation></semantics></math> suggests convergence plateau</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Wasserstein Distance</span>: Interpretation depends on label structure; focus on relative changes rather than absolute values</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I3.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A4.I3.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I3.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I3.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CRIT scores</span>: Socratic evaluation yields [0,1] range; typical threshold <math id="A4.I3.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=0.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=0.3</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS6.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Default Hyperparameters.</h5>

<div id="A4.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Standard settings: <math id="A4.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w=3</annotation></semantics></math> (moving average window), <math id="A4.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\text{stop}}=2\text{ (plateau detection)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>stop</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> (plateau detection)</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\text{stop}}=2\text{ (plateau detection)}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{I}=0.02" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.02</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{I}=0.02</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{D}=0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{D}=0.05</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{I}=\alpha_{D}=0.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>I</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{I}=\alpha_{D}=0.2</annotation></semantics></math> (reduction rates).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>CRIT: Cross-Family Argument Quality Evaluator</h2>

<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1 </span>Design Principles</h3>

<div id="A5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A5.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CRIT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>CRIT</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CRIT}</annotation></semantics></math> uses a cross-family LLM evaluator (a different model family than the debating agents) to score argument quality in <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, mitigating self-preference bias <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Panickssery et al., 2024</a>]</cite> and following the Socratic evaluation protocol <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chang [2023a]</a></cite>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Evaluation criteria.</h5>

<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Each argument is rated on three equally weighted dimensions (<math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{c}=1/3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{c}=1/3</annotation></semantics></math>):</p>
<ol id="A5.I1" class="ltx_enumerate" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.2em;">
<li id="A5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Evidence support</span>: claims backed by cited spans;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Logical coherence</span>: valid, non-contradictory reasoning;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Query relevance</span>: directly addresses the task.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Scoring process.</h5>

<div id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given debate snippet <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> with claim <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>, supporting reasons <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>, and opposing reasons <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>R</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>:
(1) validate each link <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\Rightarrow\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\Rightarrow\Omega</annotation></semantics></math> with quality <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{r}\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{r}\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>;
(2) aggregate to a composite <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma=\sum_{c}w_{c}\cdot\text{score}_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>c</mi></msub><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mtext>score</mtext><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma=\sum_{c}w_{c}\cdot\text{score}_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>;
(3) return <math id="A5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> with a brief justification.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.2 </span>Multi-Evaluator Aggregation</h3>

<div id="A5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">With <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> evaluators (default <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K{=}3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K{=}3</annotation></semantics></math>) and <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{u,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{u,t}</annotation></semantics></math> arguments from agent <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> in round <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A5.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\mathrm{CRIT}}_{u,t}=\frac{1}{N_{u,t}K}\sum_{i=1}^{N_{u,t}}\sum_{k=1}^{K}s^{(k)}_{u,t,i}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>CRIT</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathrm{CRIT}}_{u,t}=\frac{1}{N_{u,t}K}\sum_{i=1}^{N_{u,t}}\sum_{k=1}^{K}s^{(k)}_{u,t,i},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{(k)}_{u,t,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{(k)}_{u,t,i}</annotation></semantics></math> is judge <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>’s composite score for argument <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. The round-level score is</p>
<table id="A5.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CRIT}^{(t)}=\frac{1}{N_{t}K}\sum_{u}\sum_{i=1}^{N_{u,t}}\sum_{k=1}^{K}s^{(k)}_{u,t,i},\quad N_{t}=\sum_{u}N_{u,t}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>CRIT</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>u</mi></munder><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>u</mi></munder><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CRIT}^{(t)}=\frac{1}{N_{t}K}\sum_{u}\sum_{i=1}^{N_{u,t}}\sum_{k=1}^{K}s^{(k)}_{u,t,i},\quad N_{t}=\sum_{u}N_{u,t}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Using <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math> reduces single-judge variance; on our development sets we observe Krippendorff’s <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\approx 0.68" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≈</mo><mn>0.68</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\approx 0.68</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.3 </span>Reliability Weighting in MACI</h3>

<div id="A5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Exponential moving average tracks per-agent quality:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma_{u}^{(t)}=\lambda\Gamma_{u}^{(t-1)}+(1-\lambda)\,\overline{\mathrm{CRIT}}_{u,t},\quad\Gamma_{u}^{(0)}=0.5,\ \lambda=0.8." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>CRIT</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.8</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma_{u}^{(t)}=\lambda\Gamma_{u}^{(t-1)}+(1-\lambda)\,\overline{\mathrm{CRIT}}_{u,t},\quad\Gamma_{u}^{(0)}=0.5,\ \lambda=0.8.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Normalized mixture weights with stabilizer <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=10^{-6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=10^{-6}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{u}^{(t)}=\frac{\Gamma_{u}^{(t)}+\epsilon}{\sum_{v}(\Gamma_{v}^{(t)}+\epsilon)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>v</mi></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{u}^{(t)}=\frac{\Gamma_{u}^{(t)}+\epsilon}{\sum_{v}(\Gamma_{v}^{(t)}+\epsilon)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">and the final mixture is <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{(t)}(y)=\sum_{u}\omega_{u}^{(t)}p_{u}^{(t)}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>u</mi></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{(t)}(y)=\sum_{u}\omega_{u}^{(t)}p_{u}^{(t)}(y)</annotation></semantics></math>. Removing reliability weighting (uniform <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{u}=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{u}=0.5</annotation></semantics></math>) costs <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-2.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-2.0</annotation></semantics></math> pp Acc@1 (Table <a href="#S4.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ Results #2: MACI ablation. ‣ 4.1.1 Main Results, Three Parts ‣ 4.1 G1: Clinical Diagnosis ‣ 4 Empirical Validation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.4 </span>Implementation Details</h3>

<section id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Evaluator selection.</h5>

<div id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Use a skeptical, diversity-seeking judge from a different model family:
(i) for GPT-4o + Claude pairs, use Gemini 1.5 Pro as evaluator;
(ii) for Gemini pairs, use Claude 3 Opus as evaluator; temperature <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.3</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Independence.</h5>

<div id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Judges see only the argument text and minimal task context. Agent identity and opponent text are masked. Items are randomized per round.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Quality gate.</h5>

<div id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Arguments are rejected unless <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q\geq\tau_{\text{Q}}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>Q</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q\geq\tau_{\text{Q}}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> <em id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">and</em> <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CRIT}\geq\tau_{\text{CRIT}}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>CRIT</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mtext>CRIT</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CRIT}\geq\tau_{\text{CRIT}}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>; both gates tighten as <math id="A5.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="CL" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">CL</annotation></semantics></math> is reduced (Eq. <a href="#S3.E9" title="Equation 9 ‣ Information dial: raising evidence standards. ‣ 3.3 Dual-Dial Control with Plateau Detection ‣ 3 MACI: Information and Behavior Dials with Measurable Stopping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.5 </span>Example Scoring</h3>

<div id="A5.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Clinical diagnosis prompt:</span></p>
<blockquote id="A5.SS5.p1.2" class="ltx_quote">
<p id="A5.SS5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS5.p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Rate this medical argument (0--1 scale):
</span></p>
<p id="A5.SS5.p1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS5.p1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Claim: ‘‘Bilateral small-joint arthralgia favors Chikungunya over Dengue.’’
<br class="ltx_break">Evidence: [Cites CDC arboviral guidelines 2024]
<br class="ltx_break">Reasoning: Joint pain pattern is more severe and prolonged in Chikungunya.
</span></p>
<p id="A5.SS5.p1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS5.p1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Score each: Evidence support, Logical coherence, Query relevance.
</span></p>
</blockquote>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Evaluator response:</span></p>
<blockquote id="A5.SS5.p2.2" class="ltx_quote">
<p id="A5.SS5.p2.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS5.p2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Evidence: 0.90 (authoritative source cited)
<br class="ltx_break">Logic: 0.85 (valid differential reasoning)
<br class="ltx_break">Relevance: 1.00 (directly addresses diagnosis)
<br class="ltx_break">Composite: 0.92
</span></p>
</blockquote>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.6 </span>Hyperparameters</h3>

<div id="A5.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Defaults:</span> <math id="A5.SS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K{=}3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K{=}3</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.SS6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda{=}0.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda{=}0.8</annotation></semantics></math> (EMA), <math id="A5.SS6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon{=}10^{-6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon{=}10^{-6}</annotation></semantics></math>, judge temp <math id="A5.SS6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\,{=}\,0.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.448em">=</mo><mn> 0.3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\,{=}\,0.3</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.SS6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{c}{=}\tfrac{1}{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{c}{=}\tfrac{1}{3}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.SS6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\text{Q}}^{(1)}{=}0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mtext>Q</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\text{Q}}^{(1)}{=}0.5</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.SS6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\text{CRIT}}^{(1)}{=}0.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mtext>CRIT</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>0.3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\text{CRIT}}^{(1)}{=}0.3</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.7 </span>CRIT Reliability and Role in <math id="A5.SS7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MACI}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>MACI</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MACI}</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<section id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Protocol.</h5>

<div id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We adopt the <math id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CRIT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>CRIT</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CRIT}</annotation></semantics></math> evaluator with cross-family judges, identity masking, and span-grounded scoring, following the Socratic protocol. We tune on a disjoint development split and validate on a held-out set of 150 clinical-debate arguments. Judges see only the argument text, cited spans, and minimal task context. Each judge returns three sub-scores (evidence support, logical coherence, query relevance) and a composite in <math id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> with equal weights. Unless noted, 95% confidence intervals (CIs) for means are computed by nonparametric bootstrap (10,000 resamples). Proportion CIs use the Wilson method. For rank correlations we report bootstrap CIs on Fisher-<math id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math> transformed coefficients.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Inter-rater agreement.</h5>

<div id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We compute pairwise Pearson and Spearman correlations across all judge pairs, and Krippendorff’s <math id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> for overall reliability. Table <a href="#A5.T10" title="Table 10 ‣ Order invariance (𝑛=50). ‣ E.7 CRIT Reliability and Role in MACI ‣ Appendix E CRIT: Cross-Family Argument Quality Evaluator" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> shows <math id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha{=}0.68" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.68</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha{=}0.68</annotation></semantics></math> with strong pairwise correlations (Pearson <math id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.71{\pm}0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.71</mn><mo>±</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.71{\pm}0.05</annotation></semantics></math>, Spearman <math id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.69{\pm}0.04" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.69</mn><mo>±</mo><mn>0.04</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.69{\pm}0.04</annotation></semantics></math>). This level is acceptable for research use, so we employ <math id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CRIT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>CRIT</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CRIT}</annotation></semantics></math> conservatively downstream.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Judge-swap stability (<math id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n{=}100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n{=}100</annotation></semantics></math>).</h5>

<div id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We swap the primary judge family (for example, replace Gemini with Claude) on <math id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n{=}100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n{=}100</annotation></semantics></math> debates and recompute winner rankings. Depending on tie-handling for near-equal scores, the number of winner flips is either (i) <math id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k{=}2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k{=}2</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> 2.0% (Wilson 95% CI [0.55%, 7.00%]) or (ii) <math id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k{=}3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k{=}3</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> 3.0% (Wilson 95% CI [1.03%, 8.45%]). In flipped cases, score margins are small (typical <math id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|{\Delta}|\approx 0.06" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>0.06</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|{\Delta}|\approx 0.06</annotation></semantics></math>, range <math id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0.04,0.08]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0.04</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.08</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0.04,0.08]</annotation></semantics></math>), consistent with near-threshold items rather than systematic bias.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Order invariance (<math id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n{=}50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n{=}50</annotation></semantics></math>).</h5>

<div id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We reverse debater presentation order (<math id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A{\to}B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A{\to}B</annotation></semantics></math> becomes <math id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B{\to}A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B{\to}A</annotation></semantics></math>) for <math id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n{=}50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n{=}50</annotation></semantics></math> arguments. The mean absolute score difference is <math id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.038" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.038</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.038</annotation></semantics></math> (SD <math id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.024" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.024</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.024</annotation></semantics></math>), with <math id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="94\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>94</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">94\%</annotation></semantics></math> of cases showing <math id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|{\Delta}|{&lt;}0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|{\Delta}|{&lt;}0.05</annotation></semantics></math>. Spearman rank correlation between forward and reverse orders is <math id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.92" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.92</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.92</annotation></semantics></math> (95% CI [0.87, 0.95]).</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.T10" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 10: </span>CRIT reliability on 150 validation arguments with <math id="A5.T10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K{=}3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K{=}3</annotation></semantics></math> cross-family judges. Means use bootstrap 95% CIs; proportions use Wilson CIs. Judge-swap reports both <math id="A5.T10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k{=}2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k{=}2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.T10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k{=}3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k{=}3</annotation></semantics></math> outcomes for <math id="A5.T10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n{=}100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n{=}100</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
<table id="A5.T10.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A5.T10.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A5.T10.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="A5.T10.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Metric</span></th>
<td id="A5.T10.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="A5.T10.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Value</span></td>
<td id="A5.T10.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="A5.T10.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">95% CI</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T10.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A5.T10.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t" colspan="3"><span id="A5.T10.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Inter-rater agreement</span></th></tr>
<tr id="A5.T10.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A5.T10.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Krippendorff’s <math id="A5.T10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="A5.T10.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.68</td>
<td id="A5.T10.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">[0.63, 0.73]</td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T10.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A5.T10.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Pearson (avg pairwise)</th>
<td id="A5.T10.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.71</td>
<td id="A5.T10.2.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">[0.66, 0.76]</td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T10.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A5.T10.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Spearman (avg pairwise)</th>
<td id="A5.T10.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.69</td>
<td id="A5.T10.2.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">[0.64, 0.74]</td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T10.2.6" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A5.T10.2.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t" colspan="3"><span id="A5.T10.2.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Judge-swap stability (<math id="A5.T10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n{=}100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n{=}100</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></th></tr>
<tr id="A5.T10.2.7" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A5.T10.2.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Winner-flip rate (k<math id="A5.T10.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=</annotation></semantics></math>2 of <math id="A5.T10.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n{=}100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n{=}100</annotation></semantics></math>)</th>
<td id="A5.T10.2.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">2.0%</td>
<td id="A5.T10.2.7.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">[0.55%, 7.00%]</td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T10.2.8" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A5.T10.2.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Winner-flip rate (k<math id="A5.T10.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=</annotation></semantics></math>3 of <math id="A5.T10.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n{=}100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n{=}100</annotation></semantics></math>)</th>
<td id="A5.T10.2.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">3.0%</td>
<td id="A5.T10.2.8.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">[1.03%, 8.45%]</td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T10.2.9" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A5.T10.2.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t" colspan="3"><span id="A5.T10.2.9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Order invariance (<math id="A5.T10.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n{=}50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n{=}50</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></th></tr>
<tr id="A5.T10.2.10" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A5.T10.2.10.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Mean <math id="A5.T10.m16" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="|\mathrm{score}(A{\to}B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>score</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathrm{score}(A{\to}B)</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="A5.T10.2.10.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.038</td>
<td id="A5.T10.2.10.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">[0.031, 0.045]</td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T10.2.11" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A5.T10.2.11.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row"><math id="A5.T10.m17" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="-\mathrm{score}(B{\to}A)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>score</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\mathrm{score}(B{\to}A)|</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="A5.T10.2.11.2" class="ltx_td"></td>
<td id="A5.T10.2.11.3" class="ltx_td"></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T10.2.12" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A5.T10.2.12.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Spearman rank correlation</th>
<td id="A5.T10.2.12.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.92</td>
<td id="A5.T10.2.12.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">[0.87, 0.95]</td></tr>
<tr id="A5.T10.2.13" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A5.T10.2.13.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb">Cases with <math id="A5.T10.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|{\Delta}|{&lt;}0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|{\Delta}|{&lt;}0.05</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="A5.T10.2.13.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">94%</td>
<td id="A5.T10.2.13.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">[88%, 98%]</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Usage in <math id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MACI}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>MACI</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MACI}</annotation></semantics></math>.</h5>

<div id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given these properties, we use <math id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CRIT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>CRIT</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CRIT}</annotation></semantics></math> in two conservative roles: (i) <em id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">soft aggregation weights</em> for agent synthesis via <math id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{u}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{u}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> in Section <a href="#A5" title="Appendix E CRIT: Cross-Family Argument Quality Evaluator" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a> and (ii) a component of a <em id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">compound stop rule</em>. Let <math id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\Gamma}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\Gamma}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> be the mean <math id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CRIT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>CRIT</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CRIT}</annotation></semantics></math> score at round <math id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Var</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> its across-judge variance. We stop when</p>
<table id="A5.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}_{t}&lt;\varepsilon\quad\text{and}\quad|\bar{\Gamma}_{t}-\bar{\Gamma}_{t-1}|&lt;\delta," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}_{t}&lt;\varepsilon\quad\text{and}\quad|\bar{\Gamma}_{t}-\bar{\Gamma}_{t-1}|&lt;\delta,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">for two consecutive rounds,
with small thresholds <math id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon,\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon,\delta</annotation></semantics></math> selected on a development split. This couples evaluator stability with diminishing returns and prevents over-debating.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px6" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Limitations.</h5>

<div id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CRIT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>CRIT</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CRIT}</annotation></semantics></math> relies on LLM evaluators that may exhibit unknown biases or failure modes. Cross-family judging, identity masking, and span grounding mitigate these risks but do not eliminate them. Systematic validation against human experts remains important future work, especially for high-stakes deployment.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px6.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, our stability estimates likely depend on judge competence: using high-capability, cross-family LLMs to assess rubric-based “reasonableness” contributes to the observed robustness, whereas weaker or poorly aligned judges may not yield comparable results; in such settings we recommend increasing <math id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>, tightening <math id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS7.SSS0.Px6.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> in the stop rule, and adding periodic human audits.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Adaptive Initialization Strategy</h2>

<figure id="A6.T11" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A6.T11.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A6.T11.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A6.T11.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt">Condition</th>
<th id="A6.T11.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><math id="A6.T11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CL}^{(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>CL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CL}^{(1)}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<th id="A6.T11.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">Rationale</th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A6.T11.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A6.T11.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">High <math id="A6.T11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="A6.T11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;P_{70}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>70</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;P_{70}</annotation></semantics></math>), Low <math id="A6.T11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\mathrm{JS},0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>JS</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{JS},0}</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="A6.T11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;P_{30}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>30</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;P_{30}</annotation></semantics></math>)</th>
<td id="A6.T11.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">0.7</td>
<td id="A6.T11.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">High-quality, low disagreement</td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T11.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A6.T11.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Middle range</th>
<td id="A6.T11.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.8</td>
<td id="A6.T11.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">Moderate complexity</td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T11.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A6.T11.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb">Low <math id="A6.T11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="A6.T11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;P_{30}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>30</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;P_{30}</annotation></semantics></math>), High <math id="A6.T11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\mathrm{JS},0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>JS</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{JS},0}</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="A6.T11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;P_{70}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>70</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;P_{70}</annotation></semantics></math>)</th>
<td id="A6.T11.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">0.9</td>
<td id="A6.T11.2.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">Low-quality, high disagreement</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 11: </span>Development-set percentile bins for initialization. <math id="A6.T11.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>X</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{X}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes <math id="A6.T11.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>th percentile.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Before debate, we compute two signals from query and retrieved context:</p>
</div>
<section id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Initial evidence quality.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Cosine similarity between mean retrieved embedding and target prototype:</p>
<table id="A6.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{0}=\cos(\bar{\mathbf{e}}^{(0)},\boldsymbol{\theta}),\quad\bar{\mathbf{e}}^{(0)}=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{E}^{(0)}|}\sum_{e\in\mathcal{E}^{(0)}}\frac{\phi(e)}{\|\phi(e)\|}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐞</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐞</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{0}=\cos(\bar{\mathbf{e}}^{(0)},\boldsymbol{\theta}),\quad\bar{\mathbf{e}}^{(0)}=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{E}^{(0)}|}\sum_{e\in\mathcal{E}^{(0)}}\frac{\phi(e)}{\|\phi(e)\|}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}^{(0)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}^{(0)}</annotation></semantics></math> is the initial retrieved evidence set and <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝜽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> is the task-specific target prototype.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Initial disagreement.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Jensen-Shannon divergence between agents’ initial single-pass predictions:</p>
<table id="A6.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\mathrm{JS},0}=\tfrac{1}{2}\text{KL}(p_{A}^{(0)}\|m^{(0)})+\tfrac{1}{2}\text{KL}(p_{B}^{(0)}\|m^{(0)})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>JS</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mtext>KL</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mtext>KL</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{JS},0}=\tfrac{1}{2}\text{KL}(p_{A}^{(0)}\|m^{(0)})+\tfrac{1}{2}\text{KL}(p_{B}^{(0)}\|m^{(0)}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A6.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{(0)}=\tfrac{1}{2}(p_{A}^{(0)}+p_{B}^{(0)})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{(0)}=\tfrac{1}{2}(p_{A}^{(0)}+p_{B}^{(0)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.1 </span>Initialization Policy</h3>

<div id="A6.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We bin <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Q_{0},D_{\mathrm{JS},0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>JS</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Q_{0},D_{\mathrm{JS},0})</annotation></semantics></math> on development set and map to starting parameters:</p>
</div>
<section id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Intuition.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Cases with high-quality evidence and low initial disagreement likely converge quickly, so start with lower contentiousness. Cases with poor evidence quality and high disagreement need more exploration, so start with higher contentiousness.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Evidence gate.</h5>

<div id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Initial gate <math id="A6.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau^{(1)}=0.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0.3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau^{(1)}=0.3</annotation></semantics></math> for all cases. Gate rises during debate via Eq. (<a href="#S3.E9" title="Equation 9 ‣ Information dial: raising evidence standards. ‣ 3.3 Dual-Dial Control with Plateau Detection ‣ 3 MACI: Information and Behavior Dials with Measurable Stopping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>) in Section <a href="#S3" title="3 MACI: Information and Behavior Dials with Measurable Stopping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.2 </span>Robustness</h3>

<div id="A6.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This simple binning strategy is stable across:</p>
<ul id="A6.I1" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.2em;">
<li id="A6.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Encoder layer choice (late layers preferred)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Pooling method (mean vs. last-token)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Retrieval depth (<math id="A6.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{\text{ret}}\in\{16,32,48\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mtext>ret</mtext></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>32</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>48</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{\text{ret}}\in\{16,32,48\}</annotation></semantics></math>)</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Percentiles computed once on disjoint development split. After initialization, all parameter updates use live signals (<math id="A6.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathit{Q}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathit{Q}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\mathrm{JS}}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>JS</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{JS}}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{O}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{O}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CRIT}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>CRIT</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CRIT}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>) as described in Section <a href="#S3" title="3 MACI: Information and Behavior Dials with Measurable Stopping" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A7" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix G </span>Detailed MACI Case Study: Dengue vs. Chikungunya Diagnosis</h2>

<section id="A7.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.1 </span>Three-Phase Debate Walkthrough and Results</h3>

<div id="A7.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This appendix provides a complete case from the medical validation (Section <a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 G1: Clinical Diagnosis ‣ 4 Empirical Validation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>), showing how MACI’s contentiousness scheduling (<math id="A7.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>CL</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CL}</annotation></semantics></math>) and convergence control yield collaborative synthesis. Signals, weighting, and stop rules follow <span id="A7.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm</span> <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ Appendix C MACI Algorithm Specification" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Case overview.</span> Two heterogeneous agents (<span id="A7.SS1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">GPT-4o</span>, <span id="A7.SS1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Gemini 1.5 Pro</span>) jointly diagnose a patient with: skin rash, joint pain, vomiting, fatigue, high fever, headache, nausea, loss of appetite, retro-orbital pain, back pain, malaise, myalgia, and red spots. Ground truth: <em id="A7.SS1.p2.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Dengue Fever</em>. The debate follows <math id="A7.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CL}\!\in\!\{0.9,0.7,0.5\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>CL</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0.9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CL}\!\in\!\{0.9,0.7,0.5\}</annotation></semantics></math> and terminates adaptively via the relative plateau rule.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The case exhibits MACI’s three-phase trajectory (exploration <math id="A7.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> integration <math id="A7.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> consolidation). Information-theoretic evolution is summarized below (weighted JSD across agent beliefs; normalized 1-Wasserstein <math id="A7.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{W}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{W}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> between mixtures <math id="A7.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
<figure id="A7.T12" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 12: </span>Signal evolution during MACI-orchestrated Dengue vs. Chikungunya diagnosis.</figcaption>
