<section id="A7.SS2.SSS7.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Discussion</h5>

<div id="A7.SS2.SSS7.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS2.SSS7.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This example demonstrates <span id="A7.SS2.SSS7.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">MACI</span>’s principled transition from exploration to exploitation through controlled reduction in contentiousness. The initial high-entropy difference drives comprehensive exploration of diagnostic possibilities, while the gradual decrease in <math id="A7.SS2.SSS7.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>CL</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CL}</annotation></semantics></math> facilitates convergence toward a well-reasoned conclusion. Quantitative improvements in information metrics (WD decreased by 47%, MI increased by 14%, CRIT improved by 16%, and <math id="A7.SS2.SSS7.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\mathrm{JS}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>JS</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{JS}}</annotation></semantics></math> reduced by 96%) verify the effectiveness of MACI’s information-theoretic orchestration.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS2.SSS7.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Key Capabilities</h5>

<div id="A7.SS2.SSS7.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="A7.I2" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.5em;">
<li id="A7.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A7.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Transparent Reasoning</span>: Complete audit trails enable post-mortem analysis and verification.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A7.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Epistemic Humility</span>: Quantified uncertainty with actionable next steps rather than overconfident conclusions.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A7.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Training Enhancement</span>: Reasoning-rich, diverse traces that can improve future LLM performance on similar tasks.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.3 </span>Linguistic Patterns vs. Contentiousness</h3>

<div id="A7.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Rather than attempting fine-grained linguistic marker counts on limited transcript text, we analyze three clearly observable patterns that demonstrate MACI’s behavioral modulation effects:</p>
</div>
<section id="A7.SS3.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">G.3.1 </span>Pattern 1: Diagnostic Hypothesis Specificity Evolution</h4>

<section id="A7.SS3.SSS1.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Round 1 - Divergent Exploration</h5>

<div id="A7.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="A7.I3" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:0.8em;">
<li id="A7.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">–</span> 
<div id="A7.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">GPT-4: Specific viral diagnoses (Dengue, Chikungunya, Zika) with precise probabilities.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">–</span> 
<div id="A7.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Gemini: Broad categorical thinking (Viral Infection, Autoimmune Disease, Bacterial Infection).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">–</span> 
<div id="A7.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Contrast: High vs. Low diagnostic granularity.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS3.SSS1.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Round 2–3 - Progressive Convergence</h5>

<div id="A7.SS3.SSS1.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="A7.I4" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:0.8em;">
<li id="A7.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">–</span> 
<div id="A7.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">GPT-4: Maintains specificity while adding counter-argumentative language.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">–</span> 
<div id="A7.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Gemini: Rapid shift from broad categories to specific viral diseases, explicitly adopting GPT-4’s framework.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I4.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">–</span> 
<div id="A7.I4.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.I4.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Convergence: Both agents reach identical specific diagnoses by Round 3.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS3.SSS1.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS3.SSS1.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A7.SS3.SSS1.Px2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Quantifiable change:</em> Diagnostic entropy decreases from maximum divergence (broad vs. specific) to complete alignment on specific viral diseases.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS3.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">G.3.2 </span>Pattern 2: Collaborative Language Emergence</h4>

<section id="A7.SS3.SSS2.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Round 1</h5>

<div id="A7.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="A7.I5" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:0.8em;">
<li id="A7.I5.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">–</span> 
<div id="A7.I5.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.I5.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Independent assessments with minimal cross-reference.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I5.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">–</span> 
<div id="A7.I5.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.I5.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">GPT-4: “Most symptoms are classic signs…” (confident independent judgment).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I5.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">–</span> 
<div id="A7.I5.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.I5.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Gemini: Brief, categorical statements with little elaboration.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS3.SSS2.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Round 2</h5>

<div id="A7.SS3.SSS2.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="A7.I6" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:0.8em;">
<li id="A7.I6.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">–</span> 
<div id="A7.I6.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.I6.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Explicit opponent acknowledgment emerges.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I6.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">–</span> 
<div id="A7.I6.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.I6.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">GPT-4: “While viral infections can cause these symptoms…” (direct counter-argument).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I6.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">–</span> 
<div id="A7.I6.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.I6.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Gemini: “Gemini concedes to GPT-4 in the second round!” (explicit acknowledgment).</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS3.SSS2.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Round 3</h5>

<div id="A7.SS3.SSS2.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="A7.I7" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:0.8em;">
<li id="A7.I7.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">–</span> 
<div id="A7.I7.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.I7.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Collaborative assessment language.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I7.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">–</span> 
<div id="A7.I7.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.I7.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Gemini: “acknowledging the superior specificity of focusing on mosquito-borne viral diseases”.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I7.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">–</span> 
<div id="A7.I7.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.I7.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Both: Shared reasoning about diagnostic challenges (“Without additional information about geographic location…”).</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS3.SSS2.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Final Round</h5>

<div id="A7.SS3.SSS2.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="A7.I8" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:0.8em;">
<li id="A7.I8.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">–</span> 
<div id="A7.I8.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.I8.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Unified voice: “the LLMs recommend,” joint clinical suggestions.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I8.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">–</span> 
<div id="A7.I8.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.I8.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Collaborative uncertainty: “Despite moderate confidence, the system collaboratively develops…”</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS3.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">G.3.3 </span>Pattern 3: Reasoning Justification Depth</h4>

<div id="A7.SS3.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS3.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A7.SS3.SSS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Evolution of explanatory detail:</em></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS3.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS3.SSS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.SSS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Round 1:</span></p>
<ul id="A7.I9" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:0.8em;">
<li id="A7.I9.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">–</span> 
<div id="A7.I9.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.I9.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">GPT-4: 3–4 sentences per diagnosis with pathophysiological details.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I9.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">–</span> 
<div id="A7.I9.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.I9.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Gemini: 1 sentence per diagnosis, minimal elaboration.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS3.SSS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS3.SSS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.SSS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Round 2:</span></p>
<ul id="A7.I10" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:0.8em;">
<li id="A7.I10.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">–</span> 
<div id="A7.I10.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.I10.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">GPT-4: Maintains detail while adding comparative analysis.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I10.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">–</span> 
<div id="A7.I10.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.I10.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Gemini: Substantial increase in explanatory depth, diagnostic reasoning.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS3.SSS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS3.SSS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.SSS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Round 3:</span></p>
<ul id="A7.I11" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:0.8em;">
<li id="A7.I11.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">–</span> 
<div id="A7.I11.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.I11.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Both agents: Complex reasoning about differential diagnosis challenges.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I11.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">–</span> 
<div id="A7.I11.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.I11.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Shared acknowledgment of diagnostic limitations.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS3.SSS4" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">G.3.4 </span>Summary of Observable Changes</h4>

<div id="A7.SS3.SSS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS3.SSS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A7.SS3.SSS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Key finding:</em> The transcript demonstrates clear behavioral modulation effects without requiring detailed linguistic marker analysis. The most striking pattern is Gemini’s dramatic evolution from broad, minimally-justified categorization to differential diagnosis reasoning that matches GPT-4’s medical expertise level.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS3.SSS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS3.SSS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A7.T13" title="Table 13 ‣ Recommended Laboratory Tests ‣ G.2.7 Final Joint Recommendations (Convergence Achieved) ‣ G.2 Complete Debate Transcript (Round by Round) ‣ Appendix G Detailed MACI Case Study: Dengue vs. Chikungunya Diagnosis" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a> summarizes the systematic evolution across all three patterns, demonstrating MACI’s behavioral modulation effects at multiple levels simultaneously.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS3.SSS4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS3.SSS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The progression from divergent to aligned diagnostic specificity, minimal to collaborative cross-referencing, and asymmetric to symmetric reasoning depth provides qualitative evidence for MACI’s systematic behavioral modulation through <math id="A7.SS3.SSS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>CL</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CL}</annotation></semantics></math> scheduling.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A8" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix H </span>Extended MACI Case Study #2: Hepatitis Differential Diagnosis</h2>

<div id="A8.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This appendix provides a second detailed case study from the medical diagnosis validation (Section <a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 G1: Clinical Diagnosis ‣ 4 Empirical Validation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>), demonstrating MACI’s effectiveness on a harder differential (several overlapping liver-related conditions) that required extended collaboration and adaptive termination.</p>
</div>
<div id="A8.p2" class="ltx